{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem","id":1461345,"title":"[Crazy ideas] What would you want out of a 3ed of Requiem ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-25T09:59:22-07:00","id":1461345,"title":"[Crazy ideas] What would you want out of a 3ed of Requiem ?","content":"Everything is in the title, basically. What would <b>you</b> like to see in an hypothetical third edition of Requiem ? Be it lore, simple name changes for the Clans or even mechanics you think could be streamlined or something like that ?<br /> <br /> Personally, what I think we should get is the game firmly distancing itself for V:tM by ditching the names of the Ventrue, Gangrel and Nosferatu. I don't really have an idea about what to call them, of course (but I think a Latin, old Germanic and Slavic/Romanian/Hungarian would works best respectively), as as to not render the previous editions' lore about the Clans moot, we'd jsut know that Ventrue = Latin name from now on, without discounting anything said before.<br /> <br /> However, I think that over time, Requiem introduced Clans which could be used to replace entirely those three to make the setting more unique even if said Clans would also need some rework, of course. I'm not sure I'd like it in reality because it'd replace three out of them, but I think we could have :<ul><li>The Amari replacing the Gangrel in the hardy survivor slot, even if it'd mean perhaps losing the purely bestial element of the Savages to better highlight the desperate nature of the Amari</li> <li>The Pijavica taking the spot of the Nosferatu, I think they'd work really well with Nightmare even if they'd need some serious rework to be really successful and viable</li> <li>The Akhud stealing the Ventrue's throne; they are, after all, lords in their own way, and I think their Clan weakness in 2ed would make a great counterpoint to their tyrannic ways, because they wouldn't be able to betray each other directly but would spend their time trying to find was to do it so indirectly that they wouldn't trigger their weakness</li> </ul>Regardless of what they'd do with the main Clans, I'd love for the Jiang Shi to transition from possible real Clan to the youngest one. I think having them being a truly new Clan stabilizing and thus developping a new unique Discipline widely shared by its members only could be fascinating to explore. Especially if the Striges lose their shit over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T11:13:17-07:00","id":1461367,"title":"","content":"Imma be honest, I hope no clan is ever &quot;replaced&quot;. I'd rather have the clan number expanded. Don't subtract, add<br /> <br /> Though, I suppose for 3rd edition, which is pretty far off, I'd like for more mysteries of the strix to explore alongside systems (or really just lore to give you an idea) for navigating the politics of intra covenant stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T11:20:48-07:00","id":1461370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461367#post1461367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imma be honest, I hope no clan is ever &quot;replaced&quot;. I'd rather have the clan number expanded. Don't subtract, add<br /> <br /> Though, I suppose for 3rd edition, which is pretty far off, I'd like for more mysteries of the strix to explore alongside systems (or really just lore to give you an idea) for navigating the politics of intra covenant stuff</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, i would be interested in seeing alternative takes like <b>other </b>beings that NOT the Strix generating a clan or bloodline or even in something of a reversal, the Strix that we know as unintended creations of the twisted alien minds of old and demented kindred, among other possibilities to further muddy the terrain of where do the kindred come from and how do the Strix relate - or not - to them, in part or the whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T11:38:50-07:00","id":1461376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461367#post1461367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imma be honest, I hope no clan is ever &quot;replaced&quot;. I'd rather have the clan number expanded. Don't subtract, add<br /> <br /> Though, I suppose for 3rd edition, which is pretty far off, I'd like for more mysteries of the strix to explore alongside systems (or really just lore to give you an idea) for navigating the politics of intra covenant stuff</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I wouldn't want Requiem to have too many main Clans. It'd become a mess to follow and distinguish from Masquerade I think. But I'd also like the Lords, Savages and Haunts to get different names, so as to make clear that Requiem has stopped being held by his elder, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Break the blood bond Requiem, you can do it !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T11:44:24-07:00","id":1461378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461376#post1461376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I wouldn't want Requiem to have too many main Clans. It'd become a mess to follow and distinguish from Masquerade I think. But I'd also like the Lords, Savages and Haunts to get different names, so as to make clear that Requiem has stopped being held by his elder, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Break the blood bond Requiem, you can do it !</div> </div> </div> </div>I just feel it's a change that's forced more than anything, while also alienating to many long time fans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T11:53:04-07:00","id":1461382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461370#post1461370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, i would be interested in seeing alternative takes like <b>other </b>beings that NOT the Strix generating a clan or bloodline or even in something of a reversal, the Strix that we know as unintended creations of the twisted alien minds of old and demented kindred, among other possibilities to further muddy the terrain of where do the kindred come from and how do the Strix relate - or not - to them, in part or the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More muddy origins would definitively be a plus. I'd alos like to see if with the development of the Striges but also other lines Vampires could or even should get some means to fight &quot;spirits&quot; or &quot;ephemereal beings&quot;. <br /> <br /> I'm honestly torn about it. I could see Jiang Shi gaining such a Discipline, if only to make them truly distinct if they were ever promoted to full Clan status.<br /> <br /> Also, how would you think the Contagion would affect Vampires ? Could it explain their origin perhaps, since the Blood is said to be semi-alive and sentient, in a very virus way ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T12:14:31-07:00","id":1461389,"title":"","content":"I don't know, as a rule of thumb I expect the core of a new edition to stay crossover-friendly but not crossover-oriented.<br /> <br /> Changing names or the list of clans would be problematic, but holding more to their &quot;epithets&quot; may be a fair solution, using &quot;Savages&quot; and &quot;Lords&quot; as main names, with a host of common names used around that would include &quot;Ventrue&quot; and &quot;Gangrel&quot;.<br /> <br /> Adding clans would only be reasonable if there is a broad trope that isn't covered by the current combinations of clans/covenants yet in some way. I find it hard, but not impossible. But instead of creating a new clan, we could have better directions on how to do it ourselves, along with ideas and &quot;seeds&quot;, reports of things that may or not be distinct clans, along with a discussion on why to create one and how it affects the game.<br /> <br /> Muddying waters is good, and as much as I like the Strix I miss more exploration on alternative origins for the Kindred, even better with ideas on how distinct origins for each clan could still result in compatible creatures. I personally love the idea that the clans may be actually completely unrelated species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T13:11:14-07:00","id":1461406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461389#post1461389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding clans would only be reasonable if there is a broad trope that isn't covered by the current combinations of clans/covenants yet in some way. I find it hard, but not impossible. But instead of creating a new clan, we could have better directions on how to do it ourselves, along with ideas and &quot;seeds&quot;, reports of things that may or not be distinct clans, along with a discussion on why to create one and how it affects the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree wholeheartedly on this - though it's sometimes easy to forget due to similarity in terms and mechanics, clans in Requiem fill a different narrative role in relation to Masquerade. Each more like it's own &quot;undead archetype/race&quot; with a possibly time-lost origin of its own. There's a reason the &quot;extra clans&quot; are connected to optional resources, niche eras/settings or a mix of both.<br /> <br /> Different clans in some cases might be different iterations of similar phenomena and change as a society and the culture the kindred leech from for their continued existence transform with times. Not to mention what a clan is IC and OoC can be different things - in fact i would say they most definitely are, considering how some &quot;metaplot clans&quot; are awfuly similar to the Core five to the point of being potentially subsumed into them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T14:30:02-07:00","id":1461423,"title":"","content":"On not-Clan matters:<br /> <br /> 1) Not have VtR in development at the same time as CofD core 3e, so VtR does not, for the 3rd time in a row, have disparities between how the main CofD core does things and of VtR does things because parallel development leads to different solutions to the same problem, and thus rules that don't work together well (ex: Discipline use in Chase or Investigation subsystems).<br /> <br /> 2) Not really VtR only? Kill the Condition bloat. Have ~5 standardized Condition templates for mundane Conditions, and universalize common supernatural Conditions and use Disciplines to separate how Dominate inflicted Mind Control is different from Mind Arcanum inflicted Mind Control. Keep VtR only Conditions to a minimum.<br /> <br /> 3) Give Bloodline creation some easier to handle guidelines.<br /> <br /> 4) Reduce the obstacles for vampires getting into the Underworld or Shadow so they have easier crossover potential as one of the few splats without simple access to the other realms of the CofD (the day/night part is already annoying enough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T15:14:10-07:00","id":1461426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461423#post1461423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Give Bloodline creation some <s>easier to handle</s> guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be a start.<br /> <br /> Actually, I would like for Bloodlines to be completely reworked. Right now we've got three or more different broad concepts stuffed into a single, limited design space that has to compete for a singular slot on the character sheet.<br /> Like, imagine if Tremere and Scelesti were still treated like Legacies in Mage 2e. Or if Entitlements and Empty Changelings were just reduced to a set of Kiths in Changeling 2e. That'd be a huge step backwards. In my opinion, Vampire 2e should've already branched out with weirdness that does not fit the Bloodline model.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T15:29:51-07:00","id":1461427,"title":"","content":"Do people count Tilts as Conditions too when pointing out Condition bloat? Cuz I think a lot of the \u201cyou are affected by a supernatural power\u201d statuses could be Tilts, \u2018non-combat\u2019 Tilts. Save for things like Wanton, where you make knots out of the rope you were given.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines, hmm\u2026 no idea how to tinker with that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T16:25:51-07:00","id":1461431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461426#post1461426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I would like for Bloodlines to be completely reworked. Right now we've got three or more different broad concepts stuffed into a single, limited design space that has to compete for a singular slot on the character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, though I'm not sure it's as bad as the Mage and Changeling examples. I mean, I don't think it would really be a problem if the Tremere or Scelesti used up their Legacy slot by being those, because there are other ways to get bonuses for being part of a group.<br /> <br /> But I do think VtR could use some better &quot;niche weirdness&quot; support regardless of details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461427#post1461427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people count Tilts as Conditions too when pointing out Condition bloat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't, because there isn't really Tilt bloat. The Tilts are fairly set with very few additions as the CofD 2e has grown. Tilts, as they relate to powers, work like what I want to see out of Conditions. If a supernatural power cripples a limb in combat, you slap down the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt. You don't have each splat having slightly different Tilts for things like you do with Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cuz I think a lot of the \u201cyou are affected by a supernatural power\u201d statuses could be Tilts, \u2018non-combat\u2019 Tilts. </div> </div> </div>There's already plenty of this is the CofD. It comes down to my #1 point: VtR suffers because it's done in parallel with the general core book and doesn't get proper integration of these sorts of mechanics.<br /> <br /> The only problem is that &quot;non-combat Tilts&quot; are Conditions, and that's where the bloat sets in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T16:30:59-07:00","id":1461433,"title":"","content":"Integration into the core systems yeah\u2026<br /> <br /> Maybe Majesty gets \u201cimprove Impression\u201d and \u201copen Doors, but for groups\u201d powers in Social Maneuvering, while Dominate also gets \u201copen Doors of individuals\u201d and \u201cforcing Doors\u201d powers. Auspex gets Investigation powers, Celerity and Protean gets Chases powers etc. A lot of room here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T16:55:16-07:00","id":1461437,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which \u2014 and this is a drum I'll beat for the base game as well \u2014 it would be fantastic if we could get a nice granular refinement on the organization rules to play with, considering one of the most consistent angles for Requiem has been &quot;vampires as institutional corruption&quot; and 2e core makes the evocative statement of elders being conspiracies unto themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:08:23-07:00","id":1461439,"title":"","content":"Remove the need to reprint the core CofD rules in every core splatbook. I would infinitely prefer that wordcount be used on actual unique mechanics and fluff.<br /> <br /> Remove Conditions/Tilts. Maybe it works more smoothly face-to-face, but running online? Tracking Conditions/Tilts without physical cards has always been more frustration than it's worth. Never had issues with the old fashioned way of tracking buffs/debuffs.<br /> <br /> Use the freed up word count to add more campaign-building tools for GMs. Clearer rules for making custom bloodlines. More stuff like the build-a-horror rules in CofD core. More types of antagonists: Prometheans get like... three or four build-an-antagonist rules in core. Vampires get... Strix. And that's it. Maybe more guidelines on building your Domain's government, like Changelings got for Freeholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T18:04:53-07:00","id":1461450,"title":"","content":"The core rules in the core books is sort of a damned if you do, damned if you don't thing.<br /> <br /> A lot of people don't like having to juggle multiple core books, so having the main rule in ever core is useful for them. Others see it as a waste of space (esp. those of us that are big CofD fans and don't need 10 copies of the same thing).<br /> <br /> I think perhaps, for 3e, it would be nice to see two versions of at least the pdfs: ones with the core rules chapter included, and ones without. With a pdf/PoD focused distribution, it's not a huge ask even if KS based books would have to settle in one direct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T23:17:47-07:00","id":1461486,"title":"","content":"Regarding Bloodlines, I'd really like a way to design new disciplines from the ground up. It's all well and good to create a new Bloodline lore but it's really a pain in the ass to try and write entirely new disciplines... And going &quot;yep, those are gangrels but with Auspex&quot; is kinda of limitating in the long run, even if Bloodlines inflation is also a thing (but less than in 1ed).<br /> <br /> Regarding core rules, I'd actually like OPP to let translators be a little freer in what they can do. In France we don't have a translated core 2ed book. It wasn't really a problem for Requiem 2ed but when Demon was translated (the second splat to be so) we had to have the GMRU update added so it'd be playable because OPP didn't allow for an addition of the core rules in the main Demon book \ud83d\ude15.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't be against more pages overall to cover Belial Brood and possibly VII as antagonists in the core book. Strix are great but more antagonists, especially vampiric ones would be great to have at hand from the start.<br /> <br /> Edit : also, bring back a full page or two about the Unaligned/Unbound and create Lodges-like organizations for Vampires (perhaps Vampiric cults for mortals? Or gathering of very specialized Vampires like those Strix-hunters in a book, I don't remember which) and make some Unaligned-only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 09-26-2021, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:12:12-07:00","id":1461499,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much say OPP has regarding official translations of their work on IPs other companies own. Unless handling translations is part of OPP contract with Paradox (and CCP before them), translations would go through the IP owners rather than OPP. I'd love to see the CofD books in general get to a wider audience via official translations, but that's not always feasible for a number of reasons; I highly doubt OPP doesn't want it to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:21:15-07:00","id":1461504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461499#post1461499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how much say OPP has regarding official translations of their work on IPs other companies own. Unless handling translations is part of OPP contract with Paradox (and CCP before them), translations would go through the IP owners rather than OPP. I'd love to see the CofD books in general get to a wider audience via official translations, but that's not always feasible for a number of reasons; I highly doubt OPP doesn't want it to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i know that Demon was held for a long time for validation and that Agate Studio, the French translator, can't change anything, basically. But frankly, I'm already happy to have access to the books in my native language, it's a lot easier to grasp the rules that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:36:29-07:00","id":1461512,"title":"","content":"It is probable that translations stay that way because of the IP situation. The main IP is from Paradox, but OPP also have some level of copyright over the books, so any change would have to be approved by both parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:41:44-07:00","id":1461513,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think that it's what's making it harder to navigate. I also think that it's way we can expect a rather drastic change if we ever get a 3ed of CofD. I don't see Paradox wanting to have two lines too similars in lore at least, and they seem to be using rules from Requiem somewhat for V:tM, which is more popular. So i guess from a company's perspective, distancing Requiem even more could be an angle they'd use. <br /> <br /> Which i'm not sure I'd like entirely... but if it meant making Requiem more popular, I'd be able to tank it, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:46:58-07:00","id":1461515,"title":"","content":"At this point distancing them is unavoidable if we're ever to have a 3rd edition, or even new books whatsoever. V5 is already facing heavy in-house competition with V20, so keeping Requiem too close isn't going to happen unless Requiem becomes clearly a way to broaden horizons instead of self-competing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:21:24-07:00","id":1461526,"title":"","content":"Regarding what I said earlier... what do you think about Vampiric Cults ? They could be sorts of Lodges for Vampires, each geared toward a certain goal. For instance, Invictus' could focus on accumulating power and influence in certain specific sphere, with added goals (like making sure that non-Vampire controlled individuals wouldn't be able to compete with them, etc.) Of course, it could potentially step on the feet of Mekhet's Shadow Cults... It'd need to be considered carefully...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:05:23-07:00","id":1461534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461515#post1461515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point distancing them is unavoidable if we're ever to have a 3rd edition, or even new books whatsoever. V5 is already facing heavy in-house competition with V20, so keeping Requiem too close isn't going to happen unless Requiem becomes clearly a way to broaden horizons instead of self-competing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> To quote a great thinker, it'd depend if Paradox sees more Requiem as a KFC 2 or as an Albuquerque Boiled Turkey. Not gonna lie, it'd rather they go ABT and truly make Requiem more distinct; the base is already here anyway (that's why I wouldn't be bothered by name changes for the three Clans which share names with V:tM personally). I just hope we'd be able to avoid the... controversies of the V5 lore.<br /> <br /> Lacking a metaplot may help and I think writers wouldn't feel the need to gut the less savory Covenants, like the Circle of the Crone which has (thankfully) become more monstrous and inhuman in 2ed than in the 1ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T03:30:21-07:00","id":1461539,"title":"","content":"If Paradox really wants to distance the WoD and CofD.... they could always sell the CofD to OPP and then have CofD 3e use the Storypath system instead... I'm not holding my breath for that, but I'd enjoy the results.<br /> <br /> As for vampire cults? I'm not really sure how much more support that needs. What would vampire cults offer that you couldn't get out of Mystery Cult Initiation, and maybe opening up Mystery Cult Influence from Mage? Esp. that wouldn't feel redundant with Bloodlines and just the local variants of the Covenants. The Circle of Crone covers a lot of the idea of vampire cults as it is and I don't think diluting that would help the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T05:10:40-07:00","id":1461546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461376#post1461376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I wouldn't want Requiem to have too many main Clans. It'd become a mess to follow and distinguish from Masquerade I think. But I'd also like the Lords, Savages and Haunts to get different names, so as to make clear that Requiem has stopped being held by his elder, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy enough to do as things currently stand - in my own games the kindred in the nations surrounding the Baltic Sea just as frequently call shadows Grettir, haunts Lindwurm, the savages R\u00f6tgrafen and so on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly i have collected a bunch of examples of &quot;localization&quot; and alternate names in my tables out of purloined bits of lore and the occasional repurposed bloodline name among other things. Have older vampires in countries dominated by romance languages call most haunts Vermes and treat &quot;Nosferatu&quot; as a fad term used only by neonates &amp; ancillae overly influenced by modern things like cinema, undead in slavic-speaking nations referencing either Gangrel, Ventrue (or Julii) or all of them as &quot;Vedma&quot;, depending on specific country, the word Rakshasa and variants being used for haunts across all Southeast Asia....possibilities are many, many indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-26-2021, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T05:47:54-07:00","id":1461670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461546#post1461546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easy enough to do as things currently stand - in my own games the kindred in the nations surrounding the Baltic Sea just as frequently call shadows Grettir, haunts Lindwurm, the savages R\u00f6tgrafen and so on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly i have collected a bunch of examples of &amp;quot;localization&amp;quot; and alternate names in my tables out of purloined bits of lore and the occasional repurposed bloodline name among other things. Have older vampires in countries dominated by romance languages call most haunts Vermes and treat &amp;quot;Nosferatu&amp;quot; as a fad term used only by neonates &amp; ancillae overly influenced by modern things like cinema, undead in slavic-speaking nations referencing either Gangrel, Ventrue (or Julii) or all of them as &amp;quot;Vedma&amp;quot;, depending on specific country, the word Rakshasa and variants being used for haunts across all Southeast Asia....possibilities are many, many indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a very good way of changing much by changing nothing at all !<br /> <br /> I'd like the main names to change to better reflect the varied origins of the Clans but giving a wide range of names for each Clan would be great.<br /> <br /> But looking at V:tM board, what I'd like is to avoid a similar drama than the current V5 at all cost. Keep the names OPP, but spare us this madness !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T06:23:49-07:00","id":1461671,"title":"","content":"I find this a very interesting point of reflection even though I could spread a bit more further than the main discussion about clans here above.<br /> <br /> 1. I'd like to have some discipline a bit reviewed in their mechanics. I really love the concept behind every discipline, but few of them are a bit broken in how they work (rolls etc). e.g.: Auspex should be contested or more visible when used - don't like for a newbie to spot the prince, primogens etc intrigues and secrets so easily. Again, I'm fine with and I like what Auspex can do but should be more difficult to obtain the info. Same for the standard contested rolls for mental disciplines. Should be more fair the defensive roll. Vast majority of time, unless the opponent doesn't have BP 8 - 9, chance are pretty on the user side. A standard predatory aura roll, as per Majesty 1, would work indeed.<br /> <br /> 2. Art: I prefer the artistic approach of masquerade far more than requiem. I find it much more inspirational for the mood of the game AS I INTEND IT TO BE. Thus it's only my personal taste, not a judgment. I often use images and pictures from Masquerade for my campaigns although I prefer the setting and rules from requiem 2ed much more.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm fine with clans, I've grown used to the names but I could be fine to a change of such. I like Daeva in example. So I'm totally open to it. But I'd keep them low number (not strictly five, even more, but not as much as Masquerade either), and I'd like to have a bit more of lore behind any clan. Requiem in general it's a bit too open giving only rough tips - which may be fine for someone but I'd like to have some more clear detail.<br /> <br /> 4. Crit. are very hard to obtain and left pretty much to only player's will, which is taking it in calm situations just to have a beat more. I would make chance of a crit a bit higher. Not too much but passing from &quot;almost impossible&quot; to &quot;could happen&quot; so that players are not attempting to do whatever even if out of their stats.<br /> <br /> 5. Combats are quite ok but sometime are too bound to one roll. For relevant encounter I'd like to have more developed mechanics: the first who won dominate ends the combat; at high level the first who eat could send in torpor/kill the enemy in one hit (defense is pretty much useless when you get to roll 21 dice)<br /> <br /> I'll expand this post if more pops into my mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-27-2021, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:09:30-07:00","id":1461697,"title":"","content":"I haven't see the art of V5, isn't it photo-realist ? I must admit I don't like it too much myself but to each their own.<br /> <br /> Regarding the mechanics, I think a general rework would be in order indeed, even if I'm not knowledgeable enough to know which needs it the most and in which direction it'd make sense to go. In any case, if more Clans were added, it'd require more disciplines unique to them, and it'd be necessary to balance them out with the others, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 09-27-2021, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:38:19-07:00","id":1461702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461697#post1461697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't see the art of V5, isn't it photo-realist ? I msut admit I don't like it too much myself but to each their own.<br /> <br /> Regarding the mechanics, I think a general rework would be in order indeed, even if I'm not knowledgeable enough to know which needs it the most and in which direction it'd make sense to go. In any case, if more Clans were added, it'd require more disciplines unique to them, and it'd be necessary to balance them out with the others, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree about disciplines to be added if more clans would come up. Which I don't feel the needs for new disciplines. Too many powers lead to a more confusing figure of the vampire. What we have so far makes a wonderful job already and Devotions are there to mark the differences between elders making them unique.<br /> <br /> About art: yes, V5 is very photo-realistic and yet I wasn't referring to it specifically but also to previous versions. Illustrations are more creepy, more dark/goth. More close to my taste when speaking of vampire. <br /> Pictures in Requiem are, for the most part of them, drawings of comics-manga. Don't know. It does not give me back the mood and feels I have looking at Masquerade/dark age books. <br /> Requiem's Clan pictures are among the worst indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:52:57-07:00","id":1461704,"title":"","content":"Now I don\u2019t know about you lads and lasses, but I personally wouldn\u2019t mind seeing these fabled varieties of different Strix \u201ctypes\u201d 2e has occasionally alluded to..that\u2019s always intrigued me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-27-2021, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:55:12-07:00","id":1461706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461702#post1461702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree about disciplines to be added if more clans would come up. Which I don't feel the needs for new disciplines. Too many powers lead to a more confusing figure of the vampire. What we have so far makes a wonderful job already and Devotions are there to mark the differences between elders making them unique.<br /> <br /> About art: yes, V5 is very photo-realistic and yet I wasn't referring to it specifically but also to previous versions. Illustrations are more creepy, more dark/goth. More close to my taste when speaking of vampire.<br /> Pictures in Requiem are, for the most part of them, drawings of comics-manga. Don't know. It does not give me back the mood and feels I have looking at Masquerade/dark age books.<br /> Requiem's Clan pictures are among the worst indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 2ed yeah. I really liked the ones in 1ed but I found the colors didn't help 2ed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461704#post1461704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I don\u2019t know about you lads and lasses, but I personally wouldn\u2019t mind seeing these fabled varieties of different Strix \u201ctypes\u201d 2e has occasionally alluded to..that\u2019s always intrigued me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding more varieties for enemies in core book would be great, for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:32:56-07:00","id":1461729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461671#post1461671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Art: I prefer the artistic approach of masquerade far more than requiem. I find it much more inspirational for the mood of the game AS I INTEND IT TO BE. Thus it's only my personal taste, not a judgment. I often use images and pictures from Masquerade for my campaigns although I prefer the setting and rules from requiem 2ed much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must ask: which edition? The art in Masquerade varies a lot from edition to edition, sometimes book to book.<br /> <br /> V5 tends to photo-realism or photographs full-stop, but it is more than that (V20 also had a loot of this in the core, but with a very different style). I particularly hate the art of the V5 core.<br /> <br /> Tweaking mechanics is a given to happen, there's no point in a new edition without that, it's the whole purpose.<br /> <br /> One idea I can give right now for crits is for the ST that want to take the freedom to declare crit sometimes in the same way the players can do, then give them the beats. You can even have a dice roll behind the screen to decide if a given failure will turn into a crit.<br /> <br /> Names for the clans, Daeva and Mekhet are already good and unique to Requiem, Ventrue and Gangrel are the great offenders. Nosferatu is a middle point, as much as Masquerade do have the clan it is one of the most widely used names for vampire clan/type/family/whatever since the movie from 1922, so it's really no big deal to keep the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:46:05-07:00","id":1461733,"title":"","content":"On the art:<br /> <br /> Why on Earth would we want Requiem's art to be like Masquerade's art? The whole point is to give them different feels. VtM is gothic-punk. VtR is modern gothic. They should be evoking different feelings because the games have different themes to reinforce.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:02:20-07:00","id":1461740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461729#post1461729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must ask: which edition? The art in Masquerade varies a lot from edition to edition, sometimes book to book.<br /> <br /> V5 tends to photo-realism or photographs full-stop, but it is more than that (V20 also had a loot of this in the core, but with a very different style). I particularly hate the art of the V5 core.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said both V5 and previous versions I like them more than Requiem. I agree with you though, V5, among masquerade's versions, is my least favorite and yet I like its art more than requiem 2ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461729#post1461729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tweaking mechanics is a given to happen, there's no point in a new edition without that, it's the whole purpose.<br /> <br /> One idea I can give right now for crits is for the ST that want to take the freedom to declare crit sometimes in the same way the players can do, then give them the beats. You can even have a dice roll behind the screen to decide if a given failure will turn into a crit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that new edition would bring new mechanics. I was just listing what I'd like to see changing most. And it's also not always true, e.g.: Cyberpunk RED doesn't have almost anything changed in mechanics. But I still have to read it better so I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461733#post1461733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the art:<br /> <br /> Why on Earth would we want Requiem's art to be like Masquerade's art? The whole point is to give them different feels. VtM is gothic-punk. VtR is modern gothic. They should be evoking different feelings because the games have different themes to reinforce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure where you have read I was suggesting to have the two art the same... I only said that, as per my PERSONAL TASTES, I prefer Masquerade art far more. Also, I don't see any gothic mood in Requiem Art. I'd really like to have requiem art similar to The Crow, From Hell etc. Than I would love it even more than Masq. art. But it doesn't look like that to me though. Simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-28-2021, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:37:01-07:00","id":1461748,"title":"","content":"Regarding the art, it's true that Requiem's 2ed is rough over the edges... but I've grown to like it quite a lot. I wouldn't be bothered by a change, even a drastic one, but I wouldn't mind continuing with it either (then again, I only own three of 2ed books : Corebook, A Thousand Years of Nights and Secrets of the Covenants - Plus Sow the Storm or however it's called but I do\u00e0n't remember unique art for it).<br /> <br /> Regarding the mechanics, I think that on their own, Requiem's work well, but it's true that being the first splat and worked in the same time as a blue book has made it a little harder to use with others perhaps. Not as much as Demon, who really need a 2ed sooner rather than later (but not TOO soon, I haven't received my translated physical copy yet!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T14:55:09-07:00","id":1461766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461670#post1461670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's also a very good way of changing much by changing nothing at all !</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461670#post1461670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like the main names to change to better reflect the varied origins of the Clans but giving a wide range of names for each Clan would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking into the lore behind <b>why</b> i picked certain names in particular is where the slippery of lost stories and alternate origins to roll and delve into comes in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-27-2021, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T21:08:21-07:00","id":1461910,"title":"","content":"I'll make the caveat that, apart from maybe <b>Demon</b>, I think <b>Requiem Second Edition </b>is the best self-contained CofD game. It's so well made that I could run chronicles off the core book alone for the rest of my life. With that said, and in no particular order:<br /> <br /> 1. Make clash of wills more like other games -- this was addressed in the <b>Contagion Chronicle Companion</b>, so it's not a very radical suggestion, I know. It usually doesn't matter <i>within </i>a <b>Vampire</b> game, because there are subsystems to contest blood bonds and the like, but there's a couple of systems that don't play well with the other games. This is almost purely a crossover thing, though, and it's not a huge deal.<br /> <br /> 2. Rework blood sorcery. What we have is workable, but it's the mechanic I think has aged the worst in Second Edition. If nothing else, I don't think it needs to be an extended action anymore; there are other ways to represent the time sink.<br /> <br /> 3. Tweak Lashing Out and the Bestial Triad Conditions. I can't speak for everyone's experience, but I find that subsystem doesn't get used as often as it should; there's not as much incentive to use it when you have social Disciplines at your disposal, and the Willpower refresh benefit that's often brought up has one too many steps. It's not a bad system by any means, but it's a touch more finicky than it needs to be. Make it a little more simple and brutal. I also think there needs to be some sort of exception on being immune to the Conditions, especially on breaking points.<br /> <br /> 4. I actually don't think bloodlines need to change that much at base (maybe that's a hot take), but I do think we need to kill the idea of unique bloodline Disciplines once and for all (now that IS a hot take). Make all their bennies Merits and/or Devotions, and give all of them an inherent gift on top of their fourth (common) Discipline. That said, I'd also like to see some weirder sub-splat type things too. More Hollow Mekhet-esque creatures, for instance.<br /> <br /> 5. While <b>V5</b>'s Hunger system isn't QUITE what I want it to be, the idea of making Vitae more of an abstraction is a very good one. I suspect there's some way to do that with Conditions in <b>Requiem</b>. That said, there's nothing really wrong with the blood pool system, so this is more a &quot;If someone comes up with a really brilliant way to do it&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> 6. The Strix could be simplified. They're probably the best of the lot, but they suffer from some of the issues I have with the byzantine ephemeral beings system. For instance, I don't think Embodiments and Dread Powers need to be separate mechanics, or that Dread Powers need different categories at all. It's a few too many roadblocks for characters that don't track Experiences and aren't ever going to be portrayed by players, so let's remove some of them. Make them more accessible to STs, at the very least. Much like angels should probably just work like demons, Strix should probably work more like vampires, with a few caveats.<br /> <br /> VII. Give vampires ONE more way to get Willpower. Just a little one. As a treat. (I know, I know, Lashing Out, but see above.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T21:45:02-07:00","id":1461911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461910#post1461910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. While <b>V5</b>'s Hunger system isn't QUITE what I want it to be, the idea of making Vitae more of an abstraction is a very good one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with every idea you gave, actually, but this one here is special. Not more important, but special.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of the point system was the single boldest move of V5 rules-wise, along with making lesser powers free as you grow in Blood Potency, and it isn't half-bad. It pays the cost of pioneering (in context), there's clear space for improvement, but something in that line would be welcome.<br /> <br /> The system that I remember that best used this particular kind of abstraction was Mutants and Masterminds 2nd edition (I didn't liked the 3rd), so it may be a source of inspiration to tweak what V5 did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T21:52:00-07:00","id":1461912,"title":"","content":"For this potential 3e I don't propose we could also take stuff from other lines like Deviants conspiracy creation as well as the tier list, is there anything that could be taken from other gamelines that could apply to this 3e like mummy cult system?<br /> <br /> Also as heavy arms said it would be fun to have the storypath system and would very much the two games easily different from each other at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T22:13:59-07:00","id":1461917,"title":"","content":"The point with some ideas is to evaluate the worth of putting them in the core, or deciding at which book do it. If every single interesting subsystem from every game line is repeated in every book, we'll have a lot of very similar huge and expensive books with even more redundancy than we've already gotten with the rules system.<br /> <br /> Giving a core book for the rules and freeing space on the others was the one thing it should go back to 1st ed. It can even be a simpler, cheaper book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T00:04:52-07:00","id":1461924,"title":"","content":"If the page count slightly go up, I'd have no problem with more stuff in the book, but I'd rather they focus on more splat elements. While Vampires do dabble in conspiracies by nature, they are also quite insular and I think it isn't really necessary to bring them in.<br /> <br /> Instead, more page count on Covenants interplay (and intern play) could serve the same purpose lore wise without necessarily needing more specific rules. It'd be more GM guidelines than a firm system in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T01:05:37-07:00","id":1461928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461910#post1461910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Make clash of wills more like other games -- this was addressed in the <b>Contagion Chronicle Companion</b>, so it's not a very radical suggestion, I know. It usually doesn't matter <i>within </i>a <b>Vampire</b> game, because there are subsystems to contest blood bonds and the like, but there's a couple of systems that don't play well with the other games. This is almost purely a crossover thing, though, and it's not a huge deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only difference is that PGttCC includes the line that says to use an Attribute for powers that aren't dot rated. That line is actually missing from <i>all</i> core books for splats that generally use dot rated powers. MtA adds additional rules with Advanced Potency and non-standard CoWs for ephemeral entities, DtR uses +5 instead of +4 for permanent powers, both WtF and MtC uses a different trait instead of an Attribute for powers that aren't dot rated, and GtSE is the worst offender by using the activation dice pool (Attribute+Skill; no Supernatural Potency/Tolerance at all) for Ceremonies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461910#post1461910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Rework blood sorcery. What we have is workable, but it's the mechanic I think has aged the worst in Second Edition. If nothing else, I don't think it needs to be an extended action anymore; there are other ways to represent the time sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think it was good even back when Blood &amp; Smoke first came. The time required for blood sorcery (and how much that time can vary depending on your rolls) makes many rituals too impractical to use effectively. The fact that players are often reactive also means most times they know they'd benefit from a ritual, it's already too late.<br /> On top of that, the way to determine Potency introduces an extreme amount of randomness to the ritual's effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461910#post1461910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. While <b>V5</b>'s Hunger system isn't QUITE what I want it to be, the idea of making Vitae more of an abstraction is a very good one. I suspect there's some way to do that with Conditions in <b>Requiem</b>. That said, there's nothing really wrong with the blood pool system, so this is more a &quot;If someone comes up with a really brilliant way to do it&quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a good standard take (tracking resources seems to be inherently fun considering how often it shows up in popular games, and I personally enjoy it), but I can definitely see it as an optional rule included in the core just like (and possibly based on) the optional Health-as-Conditions system in VtR 2e's core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T01:59:38-07:00","id":1461931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461910#post1461910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll make the caveat that, apart from maybe <b>Demon</b>, I think <b>Requiem Second Edition </b>is the best self-contained CofD game. It's so well made that I could run chronicles off the core book alone for the rest of my life. With that said, and in no particular order:<br /> <br /> 1. Make clash of wills more like other games -- this was addressed in the <b>Contagion Chronicle Companion</b>, so it's not a very radical suggestion, I know. It usually doesn't matter <i>within </i>a <b>Vampire</b> game, because there are subsystems to contest blood bonds and the like, but there's a couple of systems that don't play well with the other games. This is almost purely a crossover thing, though, and it's not a huge deal.<br /> <br /> 2. Rework blood sorcery. What we have is workable, but it's the mechanic I think has aged the worst in Second Edition. If nothing else, I don't think it needs to be an extended action anymore; there are other ways to represent the time sink.<br /> <br /> 3. Tweak Lashing Out and the Bestial Triad Conditions. I can't speak for everyone's experience, but I find that subsystem doesn't get used as often as it should; there's not as much incentive to use it when you have social Disciplines at your disposal, and the Willpower refresh benefit that's often brought up has one too many steps. It's not a bad system by any means, but it's a touch more finicky than it needs to be. Make it a little more simple and brutal. I also think there needs to be some sort of exception on being immune to the Conditions, especially on breaking points.<br /> <br /> 4. I actually don't think bloodlines need to change that much at base (maybe that's a hot take), but I do think we need to kill the idea of unique bloodline Disciplines once and for all (now that IS a hot take). Make all their bennies Merits and/or Devotions, and give all of them an inherent gift on top of their fourth (common) Discipline. That said, I'd also like to see some weirder sub-splat type things too. More Hollow Mekhet-esque creatures, for instance.<br /> <br /> 5. While <b>V5</b>'s Hunger system isn't QUITE what I want it to be, the idea of making Vitae more of an abstraction is a very good one. I suspect there's some way to do that with Conditions in <b>Requiem</b>. That said, there's nothing really wrong with the blood pool system, so this is more a &quot;If someone comes up with a really brilliant way to do it&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> 6. The Strix could be simplified. They're probably the best of the lot, but they suffer from some of the issues I have with the byzantine ephemeral beings system. For instance, I don't think Embodiments and Dread Powers need to be separate mechanics, or that Dread Powers need different categories at all. It's a few too many roadblocks for characters that don't track Experiences and aren't ever going to be portrayed by players, so let's remove some of them. Make them more accessible to STs, at the very least. Much like angels should probably just work like demons, Strix should probably work more like vampires, with a few caveats.<br /> <br /> VII. Give vampires ONE more way to get Willpower. Just a little one. As a treat. (I know, I know, Lashing Out, but see above.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You indeed pointed out some very good point I had forgotten in my topic. I'm not fully aware about difference in clash of whills for other splats, though. Could you pls clarify the main difference?<br /> <br /> 2. Totally agreeing on BS. BS is conceptually awesome but really hard time for player to use them. And also as a narrative tool is often hard to be used without forcing the rules<br /> <br /> 3. I agree also that Lashing out is often neglected. I'd like to have it more easy go somehow.<br /> <br /> 4. I personally don't like too much all the bloodlines which came out so far but few of them as Hollow Mekhet, Kabhit etc. I think too many bloodline make them less characteristic and remarkable. I hardly use them apart Khabit and Malkovian.<br /> <br /> 5. I also like hunger concept from V5 but I think it's too randomic. When we tried V5 happened that a player could have used a lot of powers without never increasing the hunger while other in just 3 &quot;unlucky&quot; rolls was starved. Not sure how to fix it though. I also consider that Blood Point is still working fine - it's a game after all.<br /> <br /> 6. I'm not a big fan of Strix, not too much to add on this. I still use them but rarely my pg encountered a Strix not possessing anyone. Too hard to handle, especially for social/mental PC as vast majority of strix are immune to mental disciplines. <br /> <br /> I'd also like to have better clarified differentiation among Covenant and Clan life. In Masquerade was a bit more simple to handle: You belong to a certain clan, such clan may or may not pertain to Camarilla. Camarilla rules but Clans make intrigues among the Camarilla. Fair enough.<br /> Now with Covenant you have situations where, in a certain domain, you have a prince belonging to a Clan and to a Covenant, with other Covenant more or less accepted in the same Domain. You have to split your loyalty between Covenant, Clan and Prince making for PCs hard time to interpret bound to their Clan or Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-29-2021, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T02:52:13-07:00","id":1461932,"title":"","content":"In Requiem Clans are a lot less important than Covenant in the granch scheme of things because the latter gather like-minded Kindred while you can't make a choice about your Clan.<br /> <br /> I also feel that V:tM kind of corner the Market with deep Clan lore. I prefer the general idea from the Clanbooks of 1ed that a Vampire will develop along certain line according to her Clan but that such developements don't necessary mean that she'll be like others of her Clan, so to speak.<br /> <br /> All that to say I'm fine with Clans being basically a background element (that's why I never use Primogens personally... And are they even in the lexicon of 2ed?) \ud83d\ude1c","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:20:04-07:00","id":1461940,"title":"","content":"Well, to repeat myself from many a thread:<br /> <br /> Beast's Satiety system is what I'd like to see adapted to Vampire. You don't completely dump having points to spend because points are just to practical to get rid of. But you reduce the number, and use Conditions to make things a lot more interesting than the tension of running out of them.<br /> <br /> The five Condition setup with two extreme &quot;bad&quot; ones you don't want to hit if you can avoid it, and then three &quot;center&quot; ones each with its own pros and cons, combined with being inherently unstable as both spending and feeding can easily push you out of any of them, is a much more effective way to make the tension of supernatural hunger work as a gaming element. It keeps the player control of spending points with a bit of dice to keep players from having complete certainty so things remain tense. How your character deals with hunger is prominent but with a better mix of carrots and sticks instead of just rolling to see when the dice are going to start kicking your character's but just for doing stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:45:40-07:00","id":1461945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1461932#post1461932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Requiem Clans are a lot less important than Covenant in the granch scheme of things because the latter gather like-minded Kindred while you can't make a choice about your Clan.<br /> <br /> I also feel that V:tM kind of corner the Market with deep Clan lore. I prefer the general idea from the Clanbooks of 1ed that a Vampire will develop along certain line according to her Clan but that such developements don't necessary mean that she'll be like others of her Clan, so to speak.<br /> <br /> All that to say I'm fine with Clans being basically a background element (that's why I never use Primogens personally... And are they even in the lexicon of 2ed?) \ud83d\ude1c</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes they are, that said, the role of primogen has never been about being a clan representative/leader, though those things got conflated in Masquerade relatively early on, partly inspired by Chicago's - doubly ironic in that Chicago by Night <b>didn't</b> really have one member for each clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Requiem the idea of a clan leader or matriarch/patriarch does exist, but is represented by the position of Priscus. New Orleans: City of Damned in fact had a Nosferatu that filled both positions, but it's not the norm (in the NPC's own words) and the position doesn't get all that much attention in Requiem, exactly due to how the concept of clan has evolved in much different directions from Masquerade with time.<br /> <br /> <br /> The position did make an appearance in a Requiem game i participated, but that was in no small part because my elder character noticed most Gangrel in the domain were unaligned and saw a chance for networking - and kindred social experimentation, quite the asset indeed for a dragon like him - on this sort of socializing, what was partly helped by his later discovery of a whole unauthorized brood created by another demented and vitae addicted elder, his decision to &quot;adopt&quot; and teach the rogue childer serving as a excuse to draw other neonates &amp; ancilla into this teaching and exchange of ideas of his.<br /> <br /> <br /> The big punchline being that Maragato, the aforementioned elder, was never embraced, but an executed man risen from grave by the intervention of a black cat (actually a jaguar) made of shadows that would offer a bargain of sort on his dying breath - making his self-identification as Gangrel and teaching role quite questionable indeed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-29-2021, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T13:47:55-07:00","id":1462003,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I echo a desire for a reworked blood sorcery system in a hypothetical 3e. The current rules have a problem with being a little clunky and hard to actually accomplish anything with, exacerbated by most of the core book rituals [especially Cruac rituals] just not being worth the Experience investment. In all the vampire games I have played in or ST'd, only one player <i>ever</i> had a blood sorcery Discipline, and it was me. I also only used it once, because it was always more effective and interesting to solve problems with the character's other Disciplines, instead. And that feels like a really bad place for a player option to be.<br /> <br /> While we are at it, I would love if Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths were made a little more attractive, and in the case of Oaths, easier to understand. As they are, they are a little finicky and obtuse, which leads a lot of my more casual players to ignore them entirely, and either pick the Ordo Dracul if they want something special from their covenant, or accept playing a Carthian or Invictus without any of their cool toys [or just play an unaffiliated free agent]. I do not think this should be a particularly high priority for any theoretical third edition, but it would be nice to see, anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T03:27:41-07:00","id":1462107,"title":"","content":"All the Covenant perks definitvely needs some rework that's for sure. I'd also like the setting to make use of its great Absent : no Generations. I think there could be something more in here to depict that fundamental difference between V:tM and Requiem, perhaps even jsut in lore or something, I don't know. But the fact that there isn't a quasi-unpassable wall between elders and neonates in Requiem should be emphasized more to me.<br /> <br /> Perhaps not necessarily in term of hard rules with Merits and what not, but to me the elders in Requiem should be less resistant to the idea that the neonates of tonight are their heirs in many ways and so would more readily want to groom them properly. If only because, in five hundred years, they want to be able to have a proper discussion with them instead of bad-mouthed punks, so to speak !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T03:48:21-07:00","id":1462108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462107#post1462107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd also like the setting to make use of its great Absent : no Generations. I think there could be something more in here to depict that fundamental difference between V:tM and Requiem, perhaps even jsut in lore or something, I don't know. But the fact that there isn't a quasi-unpassable wall between elders and neonates in Requiem should be emphasized more to me.<br /> <br /> Perhaps not necessarily in term of hard rules with Merits and what not, but to me the elders in Requiem should be less resistant to the idea that the neonates of tonight are their heirs in many ways and so would more readily want to groom them properly. If only because, in five hundred years, they want to be able to have a proper discussion with them instead of bad-mouthed punks, so to speak !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm probably missing your point here. Why you think there should be the need of a lore adaptation to groom the neonates? I guess that it is really depending of elders' attitude how to deal with neonates and, in any case, time and centuries would teach how to behave to the former neonates more than elders could. I mean: neonates going around messing with masquerade and being disrespectful through their elders would learn that there would be consequences if they survive to the elders anger at all.<br /> <br /> I think becoming an elder is an hard task also in requiem indeed. Some players of mine is learning that as they tend to be always arrogant no matter who do they have in front of themselves, incurring in punishment, rights denied (merits blocked), up to more physical threats. I can assure the way they are acting is slowly but surely changing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would indeed like to have a superior state of vampire once they have reached or surpassed BP 10. Same way Mage has with their archmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-30-2021, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T03:57:37-07:00","id":1462110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462003#post1462003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I echo a desire for a reworked blood sorcery system in a hypothetical 3e. The current rules have a problem with being a little clunky and hard to actually accomplish anything with, exacerbated by most of the core book rituals [especially Cruac rituals] just not being worth the Experience investment. In all the vampire games I have played in or ST'd, only one player <i>ever</i> had a blood sorcery Discipline, and it was me. I also only used it once, because it was always more effective and interesting to solve problems with the character's other Disciplines, instead. And that feels like a really bad place for a player option to be.<br /> <br /> While we are at it, I would love if Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths were made a little more attractive, and in the case of Oaths, easier to understand. As they are, they are a little finicky and obtuse, which leads a lot of my more casual players to ignore them entirely, and either pick the Ordo Dracul if they want something special from their covenant, or accept playing a Carthian or Invictus without any of their cool toys [or just play an unaffiliated free agent]. I do not think this should be a particularly high priority for any theoretical third edition, but it would be nice to see, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tend to agree with this. It\u2019s not even that Oaths or Laws are bad, they\u2019re just a tad vaguely defined. With Oaths it\u2019s that the asymmetrical aspect is a little hard to wrap your head around, and Carthian Law is a bit too freeform. That\u2019s ultimately me nitpicking though; I REALLY like most of those Merits.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with Blood Sorcery is that the rituals in the core don\u2019t play well at all with the new system. I\u2019m not sure why there was such fidelity to the spells in the 1E core, especially when you look at how different the Coils are in comparison.<br /> <br /> (Is the consensus that Coils are the best covenant advantage? That\u2019s certainly my consensus. My consensus of me.)<br /> <br /> Making rituals require, like, rituals, was (IMO) thematically and narratively a really good move, I just think they should be one dice roll, and have more flexibility in when you can trigger effects once they\u2019re cast.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I actually think a few of the problems with the benefits are solved by <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>, where the rituals are much better designed around the new system and the Laws/Oaths are a lot meatier. But having to get a whole other book is a barrier of entry in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-30-2021, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:49:36-07:00","id":1462119,"title":"","content":"Coils were already broken in 1ed really. They nerfed them somewhat but it remains one of the best, if not just the best in terms of pure powers (Carthians and Invictus Merits outside of Oaths/Law are also great for roleplay purpose) yeah. And Secrets are certainly a step in the right direction, but I think it should be doable to have also a separation between ritual and spells in Blood Sorcery, as with Coils and Scales. Have rituals be powerful, well, rituals, while spells are less powerful but in instant action that Blood Sorcery masters can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T07:24:51-07:00","id":1462128,"title":"","content":"I agree about renaming or changing clans. Requiem clans work differently from Masquerade ones and the fact that there are still three Masquerade names hanging around does them a disservice.<br /> <br /> I also agree about blood sorcery. It has never worked well in Requiem. The rituals just aren't worth spending experience on, a lot of the time, because between narrow effects and the time necessary to perform them you might end up never actually using them.<br /> <br /> Finally, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said about Requiem being the first CofD gameline to be released rings true. It was like that in 1E and 2E. While Requiem 2E is obviously much better, it still bears the brunt of being the first.<br /> <br /> Sadly, with some 2E lines still unreleased, a 3E is a far-off prospect at best...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T07:52:51-07:00","id":1462130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462128#post1462128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, with some 2E lines still unreleased, a 3E is a far-off prospect at best...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter: The Vigil, the only game left that hasn't been released with the Revised Storytelling Game ruleset, has been sent out to kickstarter backers. I think there's a good chance it gets released on DTRPG before the end of the year, meaning there's nothing left to update to this edition.<br /> That said, 3E should indeed be very far away. With the RPG industry's current slow pace, it'll take many years before OPP gets through the life cycles of the current edition of Deviant, Mummy and Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:44:09-07:00","id":1462165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462110#post1462110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Is the consensus that Coils are the best covenant advantage? That\u2019s certainly my consensus. My consensus of me.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462119#post1462119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it should be doable to have also a separation between ritual and spells in Blood Sorcery, as with Coils and Scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be similar to VtM's Paths and Rituals, which I actually think is a good starting point. As much as access to rituals is a benefit in itself, the lack of basic effects for Cr\u00faac and Theban harms them a lot.<br /> <br /> For my games I think I'm going to rewrite the ritual paths with some MtAw 2nd inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T19:33:35-07:00","id":1462202,"title":"","content":"Must admit i'm just throwing around a random through that just crossed my mind, but is there anything in common, parallel or form of connection-relation between Invictus Oaths and Fae Contracts?<br /> <br /> Because it could lead into some pretty weird places depending on the actual answer i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:04:03-07:00","id":1462205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462202#post1462202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must admit i'm just throwing around a random through that just crossed my mind, but is there anything in common, parallel or form of connection-relation between Invictus Oaths and Fae Contracts?<br /> <br /> Because it could lead into some pretty weird places depending on the actual answer i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d go for Fae pledges instead, as some sort of pseudo-oaths. Maybe the first formation of the First Estate wasn\u2019t entirely a vampire-only business\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:27:46-07:00","id":1462209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462205#post1462205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d go for Fae pledges instead, as some sort of pseudo-oaths. Maybe the first formation of the First Estate wasn\u2019t entirely a vampire-only business\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>There's my lack of familiarity with the subject showing. Yes, thanks. That might lead into some very interesting permutations, interactions - and questions - about the Covenant's roots as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:36:15-07:00","id":1462211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462209#post1462209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's my lack of familiarity with the subject showing. Yes, thanks. That might lead into some very interesting permutations, interactions - and questions - about the Covenant's roots as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn\u2019t trying to point out anyone\u2019s lack of familiarity over anything. Just felt that the reciprocal liege-vassal relationship levied by the Invictus Oaths is more similar to pledges than Contracts. Also, the freeform and individualized nature of pledges parallels nicely with the ritual Disciplines and Coils.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I\u2019m wondering if Carthian Laws could be related to/ modeled after Old Laws of Dead Dominions. And I swear, <i>someone</i> spoke of this idea before in the forums, though I can\u2019t remember whom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:47:24-07:00","id":1462214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462205#post1462205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d go for Fae pledges instead, as some sort of pseudo-oaths. Maybe the first formation of the First Estate wasn\u2019t entirely a vampire-only business\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the same when I read about the Oaths the first time, but never got myself to work something in this line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:00:28-07:00","id":1462216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462211#post1462211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I wasn\u2019t trying to point out anyone\u2019s lack of familiarity over anything. Just felt that the reciprocal liege-vassal relationship levied by the Invictus Oaths is more similar to pledges than Contracts. Also, the freeform and individualized nature of pledges parallels nicely with the ritual Disciplines and Coils.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I\u2019m wondering if Carthian Laws could be related to/ modeled after Old Laws of Dead Dominions. And I swear, <i>someone</i> spoke of this idea before in the forums, though I can\u2019t remember whom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those ideas put together can bring a lot of <b>huge</b> questions and unexpected crossover elements to one's Requiem table indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T02:32:33-07:00","id":1462256,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, something I just though about... Don't overuse the first-person information in the books. I really like Secrets of the Covenants but it's really hard to find information in here quickly ebcause of it's First-person narration for all the lore bits. Adding some is definitively a good idea to present more PoV, but just not overdoing it is better overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462216#post1462216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those ideas put together can bring a lot of <b>huge</b> questions and unexpected crossover elements to one's Requiem table indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall, using more outside Vampire elements for Each Covenant could be great to tie the game more to the wider CofD universe. The Lancea's powers being tied to the God-Machine Angels perhaps explaining why they have to destroy stuff to use them (a sort of sacrificial Infrastructure perhaps), the Ordo being tied to Deviants/Prometheans, etc. <br /> <br /> Without adding like three pages of fluff about it. But hinting atthose more directly could be interesting I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 10-01-2021, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T04:34:21-07:00","id":1462264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462256#post1462256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, using more outside Vampire elements for Each Covenant could be great to tie the game more to the wider CofD universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hints and potential but not stated out connections are good enough for STs to tailor the degree of crossover or not in their chronicles according to familiarity and preferences.<br /> Makes it easier to keep the players guessing and invested in exploring the mystery, i think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462256#post1462256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea's powers being tied to the God-Machine Angels perhaps explaining why they have to destroy stuff to use them (a sort of sacrificial Infrastructure perhaps),</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, that sounds so mindbogglingly obvious in hindsight when pointed out it's even funny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462256#post1462256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Ordo being tied to Deviants/Prometheans, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little lost here, but then i know little to nothing about Deviants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462256#post1462256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without adding like three pages of fluff about it. But hinting at those more directly could be interesting I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But speaking of hints, let me go back to exploring the Owls' elusive supposed connection to kindred origins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Have ever noticed how the Strix changed in a number of ways between their debut in Requiem to Rome and contemporary materials? There's much that stayed but lots of changed details, bits of description (once only owls, but nowadays owls, ravens, vultures or <i>other birds of ill-omen</i>, you know), motives and much more. One might even consider the possibility of there being multiple beings under the &quot;strix&quot; label, much like not all &quot;vampires&quot; or even &quot;kindred&quot; are created equal or even from a common origin. Birds of a different feather, do flock together sometimes... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Check out the sparrows from Shadows of UK if you can.<br /> <br /> <br /> But now speaking different degrees of directedness with hints, just in case my previous paragraph was a little hermetic &amp; obtuse , there's this fun box in one of the 1e books:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Originally posted by <b>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead, pg. 120</b></i><br /> <b><i>The Owl, Night's Herald</i></b><br /> <i>It's worth taking a look at owls as a symbol, to understand what they - and, by proxy, what the Strix - can represent. Owls are:<br /> <br /> - Ill-omens, or omens of death. Certain native peoples in India believe they foretell an individual's death.<br /> Pliny the Elder believed they signal death, though not just on the personal scale.<br /> In Borneo, they're seen as creatures that bring bad luck.<br /> <br /> - Symbols of death. Different than &quot;omens&quot; of death, here it's assumed that owls are simply beasts with a sympathy toward all things dead.<br /> They gather in graveyards, they haunt the trees outside a room where a person died. In Navaho myth, they're sometimes assumed to be ghosts.<br /> Some myths have them as psychopomps, shuttling souls from this world to the underworld.<br /> <br /> - Betrayers. In China, myth (falsely) states that owlets pluck out the eyes of their mothers with hungry beaks.<br /> <br /> - Occult forces. Shamans sometimes &quot;learn&quot; spells from owls. Their terrible &quot;devil bird&quot; shrieks are said to cause madness due to an owl's sympathy with the demonic.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, after reading this box in the book back then, i experimented with alternatives, eerie black cats, glittering spirit snakes, somber hellhounds or silver-tongued beings dressed in the guise of one's own broken reflection or maybe skull-faced Grim Reaper itself, who will offer a mockery of life and power as blood-drinking undead to those ambitious, desperate or perverted enough to pay the peculiar prices of their favors.<br /> <br /> Or, being a little more descriptive:<br /> <br /> - A lineage of Japanese vampires originated from a pact with nekomata, in the vein of the strix/julii backstory.<br /> <br /> - An old medieval tale speaks of a witch that was brought back from death by her black cat familiar, who tricked Death itself into striking at his mistress' mirror image instead of herself, taking the broken shards of her reflection in place of her life and it is for this reason the kindred lack of a reflection. Since that event Death has hunted, from the other side of mirrors, for that woman and all those of her undead brood. And every time a vampire exerts their will in making itself visible in a mirror, the Reaper (Baykosh) gets a little closer to finding that childe.<br /> <br /> - The &quot;Gangrel&quot; elder i previously mentioned? Initially i was just riffing &quot;dying person made into a Jullii by the strix&quot; bit of lore but reskined it with black cats - and witches - in place of owls for a character's backstory. Later on i found out the Kanaima, vengeance spirits that rise the corpses of shades consumed with a desire for justice or redress, in pages 67-71 of the Skinchangers bluebook and developed those feline strix expies further, with personalities and priorities very much their own. Wrapping up the connection with a <i><b>Bruxa </b></i>NPC (Cihuateteo) while at it, since the jaguar is already cited as one of their patrons in Wicked Dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> And now i ask you people - how many of those symbolisms/themes do not <b><i>also </i></b>fit with the sparrows in the isles folklore?<br /> Who's to say they have not played games of their own with the living and the dead?<br /> <br /> Though these symbolisms/occult resonances are far from unique to birds - cats, dogs, serpents or other animals, sometimes even things or events, like a distorted reflection in a broken mirror (for a link to Bloody Mary or Red Jack), a peculiarly colored or shaped moon, solar eclipse or more have been saddled with such associations. Check out the <i>Kanaima </i>in pages 67-71 of Skinchangers. The strix do not have to be particularly unique.<br /> <br /> Also, the Beasts of Bethlehem (from pages 115-117 of Antagonists), for something that could work as a form taken by Bale Hounds after death, a Nosferatu-specific strix surrogate - or who knows, even both. Maybe that's what the little birds are guiding the Sparrowclaw Circle from Shadow of UK towards becoming?<br /> <br /> Or paraphrasing from a colleague's comment in an older topic...<br /> <br /> <i>What if the rumored vampires lurking with golden eyes at the edges of kindred society of Britain haven't a clue what you speak of when the &quot;owls of dis&quot; are brought up?</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Or ask back <i>&quot;Don't you mean the hounds?&quot;</i> instead - what does one make of it?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> What does a vampire do when the face it stares at in a broken mirror, the one that should be its own, shows eyes that shine in a different sheen and speaks with its voice but words not its own?<br /> <br /> There's much that may lurk at the edge of shadows - or be nothing beyond a trick of the light. That's for the brave - or fateful - to find out. Or meet their doom trying.<br /> <br /> <br /> Me i'm partial to twisted things, where the patterns we expect to see are broken down and take new forms.<br /> <br /> Like how the &quot;modern&quot; strix brewing trouble around might not be the original &quot;real&quot; thing, but an ironic byproduct of some crazed &quot;Gangrel/Julii/Ventrue/whoever made the Unholy&quot; twisted propitiation rites <b><i>giving form</i></b> to what they would supposedly keep away.<br /> <br /> <br /> How the Cihatuateteo change from an elusive two-clan bloodline/shadow cult in Shadows of Mexico to a group of mortal almost immortal blood witches in Wicked Dead. But both things might be true <i>if every Cihuateteo vampire was an spontaneous risen dead Cihuateteo witch</i>, their &quot;clan&quot; an artifact of which entity, Jaguar or Whore, was their patron/mentor. From mortal to self-made &quot;ghoul&quot; witch to sireless vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or alternatively, sparrows that might train and tame the bale hounds, whose twisted nature in death generate Bethlehem Beasts/Hellhounds that terrorize places of atrocity and fear in death, sometimes messing their human prey so badly those that die from fear rise back as worms of sorts, undead things made fat on fear themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> And so it goes, a slippery slope of hooks and dots for one to connect in ever more elaborate or bizarre images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T08:50:29-07:00","id":1462284,"title":"","content":"I think it's importants the Theban Sorcery remains mysterious. Faith is a significant theme for the Lancea et Sanctum and there's a possibility that Theban Sorcery does come from God as they know Him. This would support the dread implication that Dr. Caroline Petronius raises at the end the <i>Testament of Longinus</i>. Or it might be a big, flashy stick that isn't godly in any way, that serves nothing but the will of the sorcerers themselves. Or it could be a force they don't understand with consequences that they don't know. And so on.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T11:13:27-07:00","id":1462296,"title":"","content":"In general, I would want a hypothetical 3e to avoid mixing splat lore. The Arcadia drama between Changeling and Mage is one key reason why. Another is that a lot of people (myself included) prefer the toolkit method of setting info that CofD provides over cWoD. The more setting gets set in stone, the less use I have for it. The way 2e provides several suggestions but ultimately says 'nobody knows' is ideal, though Changeling 1e doing just that was enough to cause Mage fans to get upset.<br /> <br /> Finally, while I advocate strongly for not reprinting core rules in every splat, I think every splat should otherwise stand alone and not require learning the lore and setting details of all the others to understand.<br /> <br /> CofD is a universe with many, many strange things happening. Cross-pollinating the sources of those strange things just makes everything seem a little less strange and a little more the product of a few well-known phenomena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:59:10-07:00","id":1462356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462296#post1462296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I would want a hypothetical 3e to avoid mixing splat lore. The Arcadia drama between Changeling and Mage is one key reason why. Another is that a lot of people (myself included) prefer the toolkit method of setting info that CofD provides over cWoD. The more setting gets set in stone, the less use I have for it. The way 2e provides several suggestions but ultimately says 'nobody knows' is ideal, though Changeling 1e doing just that was enough to cause Mage fans to get upset.<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> CofD is a universe with many, many strange things happening. Cross-pollinating the sources of those strange things just makes everything seem a little less strange and a little more the product of a few well-known phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just a nod here and there, just enough for people to draw lines only if they want to, probably suffices. Like, a line or two about a marble-skinned gentleman who is strict with promises could easily be referring to some sort of fae creature, but is even more likely to be an old vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T17:29:54-07:00","id":1462364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462264#post1462264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little lost here, but then i know little to nothing about Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviant and Promethean are the two most obviously Mad Science Adjacent splats, is the probable connection there.<br /> <br /> I can take or leave crossover hooks (&quot;grotesque alchemy&quot;/&quot;the Curse is a turning key, and it has so many teeth&quot; carries me quite a ways on its own as a functional Voice of the Angel for Blood and Smoke), but building out the ways in which you can spin a bloodline out of the Curse absorbing smaller curses would be great, as would a little more material for interconnecting lines of descent.<br /> <br /> And, of course, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1420717-game-design-disciplines-how-and-why\">making the Discipline/Devotion development process more of a thing</a>, mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T17:57:34-07:00","id":1462367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462364#post1462364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant and Promethean are the two most obviously Mad Science Adjacent splats, is the probable connection there.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little loose, but makes sense indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462364#post1462364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can take or leave crossover hooks (&quot;grotesque alchemy&quot;/&quot;the Curse is a turning key, and it has so many teeth&quot; carries me quite a ways on its own as a functional Voice of the Angel for Blood and Smoke), but building out the ways in which you can spin a bloodline out of the Curse absorbing smaller curses would be great, as would a little more material for interconnecting lines of descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, overall i'd say you're much more up to date on 2e lore &amp; mechanics than <b>me</b>, for whatever it's worth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T22:16:33-07:00","id":1462399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462256#post1462256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, something I just though about... Don't overuse the first-person information in the books. I really like Secrets of the Covenants but it's really hard to find information in here quickly ebcause of it's First-person narration for all the lore bits. Adding some is definitively a good idea to present more PoV, but just not overdoing it is better overall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, using more outside Vampire elements for Each Covenant could be great to tie the game more to the wider CofD universe. The Lancea's powers being tied to the God-Machine Angels perhaps explaining why they have to destroy stuff to use them (a sort of sacrificial Infrastructure perhaps), the Ordo being tied to Deviants/Prometheans, etc.<br /> <br /> Without adding like three pages of fluff about it. But hinting atthose more directly could be interesting I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See I always thought that Theban was in someway related to Mummy and Duat considering it's egyptian motifs and the white ashes you get after using an object as a sacrament. I thought it was like sending something to the Underworld/Duat. In 2e it seems like it might make even more sense with mummies not experience time in a linear fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T03:36:24-07:00","id":1462416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462399#post1462399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See I always thought that Theban was in someway related to Mummy and Duat considering it's egyptian motifs and the white ashes you get after using an object as a sacrament. I thought it was like sending something to the Underworld/Duat. In 2e it seems like it might make even more sense with mummies not experience time in a linear fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know anything about Mummies ... How do they work ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T07:59:31-07:00","id":1462424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462399#post1462399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I always thought that Theban was in someway related to Mummy and Duat considering it's egyptian motifs and the white ashes you get after using an object as a sacrament. I thought it was like sending something to the Underworld/Duat. In 2e it seems like it might make even more sense with mummies not experience time in a linear fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342852-origins-of-theban-sorcery?p=1347302#post1347302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the spirit of being retired, I always considered that the writings Amoniel led the vampires to... Were Utterances.</div> </div> </div> </div>(^ Headcanon from former Mage lead dev who's worked with all twelve CofD games.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T08:53:16-07:00","id":1462429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross splat lore does not particularly strike me as something a theoretical third edition realistically has to address or curtail. As it does not actually appear to be be much of an issue. Cross dark eras and other material sometimes has setting threads but nothing substantial, problematic or WoDesque. The Arcadia thing feels way more a fandom issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, very much a rabid fandom issue, like there were a bunch of those between MtAw and WtF fans before that, if memory tricks me not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T08:44:07-07:00","id":1462556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462424#post1462424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (^ Headcanon from former Mage lead dev who's worked with all twelve CofD games.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess Utterances are some important element of Mage lore ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T09:20:59-07:00","id":1462557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462556#post1462556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess Utterances are some important element of Mage lore ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Utterances are the main powers of mummies. I just included some info about Dave Brookshaw for those who don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T09:25:24-07:00","id":1462558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462557#post1462557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Utterances are the main powers of mummies. I just included some info about Dave Brookshaw for those who don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh ! Nice ! Yeah, Mummy lore in Thebes would also makes sense (well, Egyptian Thebes since there was also a Greek one ^^).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T08:41:34-07:00","id":1463424,"title":"","content":"Upping this because we talked about the art and it'd obviously be a part of the 3ed of Requiem if it ever happens, and this article brought me back to it : <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/official-v5-art-packs-for-storytellers-vault-and-dark-pack-creators\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news...-pack-creators</a><br /> <br /> And it made me realize that I'd love for a return of the black and white art of 1ed, or perhaps a mix of it and the current art, albeit refined, to be slightly less rough over the edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T06:07:21-07:00","id":1465505,"title":"","content":"What I'm about to write is basically anathema for most of the vampire fanbase and I'm fully prepared for any rant that might come but personally, I think that a way to allow vampires to better withstand the sun would be nicer if only for the purpose of a multisplat game, I've played the lone vampire in such a game and the sunlight limitation was a problem. As of now, vampires get more damaged by the sun for every level of humanity they have and with higher frequency based on their blood potency, this means that a blood potency one vampire takes 1 point of lethal damage every 10 minutes of exposure, while this is somewhat manageable (fear frenzy is still an issue of course) the more your blood potency grows, the more damage per turn you take, this basically force a player to keep his vampire at a maximum of 2 blood potency dot or risk getting dusted the second he poke his nose in the sun. I've played a 1 year campaign where, at the conclusion of every chronicle, there would be a time skip of a few decades, my character automaticaly got a dot of blood potency for every 50 years (as the rulebook says) and this proved to be a real pain for everyone involved. My suggestion would be to either remove or at least increase the damage per turn brought by blood potency or have other means to mitigate (never remove) the problem, I know it looks stupid but thicker clothing to keep sun damage at bay for a couple of minutes or so wouldn't be unreasonable to me. To balance this the vampire who operates in the morning should get a dice penaly to all his actions during the day and all his disciplines should be capped by his blood potency (a bp 1 vampire could only use the first dot of his disciplines for example), this would make operating in the daylights a very dangerous endeavour for vamps but it would still allow for a minimum of activity instead of keeping a player still untill the sun rises. I know that the ordo dracul have coils for this but not every player character is going to be an ordo dracul in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T08:08:10-07:00","id":1465513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465505#post1465505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm about to write is basically anathema for most of the vampire fanbase and I'm fully prepared for any rant that might come but personally, I think that a way to allow vampires to better withstand the sun would be nicer if only for the purpose of a multisplat game, I've played the lone vampire in such a game and the sunlight limitation was a problem. As of now, vampires get more damaged by the sun for every level of humanity they have and with higher frequency based on their blood potency, this means that a blood potency one vampire takes 1 point of lethal damage every 10 minutes of exposure, while this is somewhat manageable (fear frenzy is still an issue of course) the more your blood potency grows, the more damage per turn you take, this basically force a player to keep his vampire at a maximum of 2 blood potency dot or risk getting dusted the second he poke his nose in the sun. I've played a 1 year campaign where, at the conclusion of every chronicle, there would be a time skip of a few decades, my character automaticaly got a dot of blood potency for every 50 years (as the rulebook says) and this proved to be a real pain for everyone involved. My suggestion would be to either remove or at least increase the damage per turn brought by blood potency or have other means to mitigate (never remove) the problem, I know it looks stupid but thicker clothing to keep sun damage at bay for a couple of minutes or so wouldn't be unreasonable to me. To balance this the vampire who operates in the morning should get a dice penaly to all his actions during the day and all his disciplines should be capped by his blood potency (a bp 1 vampire could only use the first dot of his disciplines for example), this would make operating in the daylights a very dangerous endeavour for vamps but it would still allow for a minimum of activity instead of keeping a player still untill the sun rises. I know that the ordo dracul have coils for this but not every player character is going to be an ordo dracul in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being covered by clothes already lower the BP level for the purpose of counting damages. <br /> I think that, going too far through this path would lead to something I really hate when talking of vampires media: vampire covering themselves with solar cream, sunglasses and large coats, being then able to act as normal people.<br /> Sun must to be what it is for them: anathema. Something to be feared of the most <br /> <br /> Also, acting during day it's already providing from a minimum of 2 dice to 4 dice of penalty just for being active instead to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> I think it works pretty much fine as it is and starting to taking out what characterize a vampire (or any other race) for the sake to play all together with other splats, take out a lot of the depth of this setting.<br /> <br /> I would instead go for Vampire's players using their ghouls during day while the main character slumber till night when he will awake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T08:52:19-07:00","id":1465517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465513#post1465513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being covered by clothes already lower the BP level for the purpose of counting damages.<br /> I think that, going too far through this path would lead to something I really hate when talking of vampires media: vampire covering themselves with solar cream, sunglasses and large coats, being then able to act as normal people.<br /> Sun must to be what it is for them: anathema. Something to be feared of the most<br /> <br /> Also, acting during day it's already providing from a minimum of 2 dice to 4 dice of penalty just for being active instead to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> I think it works pretty much fine as it is and starting to taking out what characterize a vampire (or any other race) for the sake to play all together with other splats, take out a lot of the depth of this setting.<br /> <br /> I would instead go for Vampire's players using their ghouls during day while the main character slumber till night when he will awake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the game I played clothes didn't lower the BP for solar damage, is it written in the core book or its a supplement? I'm not a writer so I don't have an easy answer to this, but as to how things are now, a multisplat game including vampires will either have to be played during night hours or exclude vampires altogether, I'm not saying you have to go the way of the matrix with vampires dressing in trenchcoat and sunglasses but I can tell you that in most of the multisplat games I played (and I played quite a few) the ST didn't want vampires in the group due to the limitations they brought. Even playing as a ghoul will mean creating a second character with attributes and traits which translate for even more work for the story teller, and would also mean that the vampire character won't get as many beats as the other players since the ghoul would be doing most of the day work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:43:50-07:00","id":1465521,"title":"","content":"Coverage is in the core book. While I am less anti-crossover than many here, and have run a mixed game over a period of years in the past, damaging the integrity of a splat for the sake of crossover isn't good for anybody. A much simpler solution that doesn't weaken the vampiric themes of Vampire would be to simply say all the characters have day jobs and you can't do your adventuring/investigating until the sun goes down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:46:34-07:00","id":1465523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465517#post1465517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the game I played clothes didn't lower the BP for solar damage, is it written in the core book or its a supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally the last paragraph in the section on sunlight damage before the charts: &quot;A character can avoid damage from sunlight only with complete coverage from its rays. If she only exposes her eyes, for example to run for shelter, consider her Blood Potency one step lower on the chart.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:52:39-07:00","id":1465525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465523#post1465523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's literally the last paragraph in the section on sunlight damage before the charts: &quot;A character can avoid damage from sunlight only with complete coverage from its rays. If she only exposes her eyes, for example to run for shelter, consider her Blood Potency one step lower on the chart.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought that coverage meant being in a car with darkened windows or indoor not being fully clothed, does this mean that covering with a uv reflective tarp would protect from damage? I think masquerade has something like this but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T09:58:08-07:00","id":1465526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465521#post1465521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coverage is in the core book. While I am less anti-crossover than many here, and have run a mixed game over a period of years in the past, damaging the integrity of a splat for the sake of crossover isn't good for anybody. A much simpler solution that doesn't weaken the vampiric themes of Vampire would be to simply say all the characters have day jobs and you can't do your adventuring/investigating until the sun goes down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I proposed a similar solution multiple times and no ST agreed to that, the reasons were varied but the most simple is that keeping the game to the 8-9 hours limit a vampire would be to limiting for extended actions and the like. From what I gather, not even the fanbase mind not being able to multi splat with a vampire so Its fine I guess, just throwing the idea around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T10:44:22-07:00","id":1465530,"title":"","content":"1- In the original novel Dracula is absolutely able to meet the sun as much as he wants. Some of his powers can't be used during the day and that's about it. Although thematic, a Vampire's weakness to the sun is a later development, isn't an inherent theme of the trope and I think it is strongly overestimated. People take more damage from the thought of it than early vampires ever took from the sun.<br /> <br /> 2- An ST that can't bend a merely thematic rule for the ease of play is making a bad decision. Forcing this one single player to play with a Ghoul or to be out of commission for most of the game is really necessary? Forbidding the splat entirely is a reasonable approach to this? In my first crossover game, back in cWoD, the Theurge PC sought a servant of Helios and made me a fetish hat that protected me from the sun. And that was that, so we could play without any problems.<br /> <br /> 3- You can find a middle ground, it is not about just ignoring the sun. A person that needs to use heavy clothes in a sunny day stands out. A character that needs to devote a few dots to a Discipline or something is paying a price. As long as there is some effort, what's the frigging problem? The Trench Coat Brigade will have to avoid the fire even more if it means not only fire damage, but also clothes damage and sun exposure, just to cite one example.<br /> <br /> 4- That all said, I do understand that putting things in the core book is tricky. If it sounds easy, even if it isn't supposed to, it will be abused on non-crossover games. Adding sun resistance is easier than taking it out. But I do think some thought can be given to this, even if it is just a recommendation in the storytelling section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T10:57:14-07:00","id":1465532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465530#post1465530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- In the original novel Dracula is absolutely able to meet the sun as much as he wants. Some of his powers can't be used during the day and that's about it. Although thematic, a Vampire's weakness to the sun is a later development, isn't an inherent theme of the trope and I think it is strongly overestimated. People take more damage from the thought of it than early vampires ever took from the sun.<br /> <br /> 2- An ST that can't bend a merely thematic rule for the ease of play is making a bad decision. Forcing this one single player to play with a Ghoul or to be out of commission for most of the game is really necessary? Forbidding the splat entirely is a reasonable approach to this? In my first crossover game, back in cWoD, the Theurge PC sought a servant of Helios and made me a fetish hat that protected me from the sun. And that was that, so we could play without any problems.<br /> <br /> 3- You can find a middle ground, it is not about just ignoring the sun. A person that needs to use heavy clothes in a sunny day stands out. A character that needs to devote a few dots to a Discipline or something is paying a price. As long as there is some effort, what's the frigging problem? The Trench Coat Brigade will have to avoid the fire even more if it means not only fire damage, but also clothes damage and sun exposure, just to cite one example.<br /> <br /> 4- That all said, I do understand that putting things in the core book is tricky. If it sounds easy, even if it isn't supposed to, it will be abused on non-crossover games. Adding sun resistance is easier than taking it out. But I do think some thought can be given to this, even if it is just a recommendation in the storytelling section.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, I never understood this wall toward multisplat with vampires, you would think rules could be bent a little but I assure you that, save that single game I played, most of the storytellers absolutely refused to have vampires in the chronicle and I understand their point of view, not being able to stand sunlight is a pretty big limitation and not something you could work around easily. I'm kinda bummed about it because there is something special about the way vampires play, it would fit neatly into a classic multisplat with a werewolf as the combat monster, a mage as reality warper intellectual and the vampire as the people specialist, CoD prides itself in being more rules friendly toward multi splat gaming and thats true for all them except the vampires, a shame really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T11:00:11-07:00","id":1465533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465517#post1465517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In the game I played clothes didn't lower the BP for solar damage, is it written in the core book or its a supplement? I'm not a writer so I don't have an easy answer to this, but as to how things are now, a multisplat game including vampires will either have to be played during night hours or exclude vampires altogether, I'm not saying you have to go the way of the matrix with vampires dressing in trenchcoat and sunglasses but I can tell you that in most of the multisplat games I played (and I played quite a few) the ST didn't want vampires in the group due to the limitations they brought. Even playing as a ghoul will mean creating a second character with attributes and traits which translate for even more work for the story teller, and would also mean that the vampire character won't get as many beats as the other players since the ghoul would be doing most of the day work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even not being a vampire, and in real world, most of the &quot;underground&quot; affairs happens at night for plenty of reasones. That's said, to have a second sheet for a player is honestly not so much of a deal for any willing ST.... Is like having a player more and you could also consider to use an NPC or a simplified sheet <br /> <br /> The beats can be, with a bit of flexibility, still being addressed to the main character (maybe with the exception of those coming from damages or conditions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T11:21:45-07:00","id":1465535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465533#post1465533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even not being a vampire, and in real world, most of the &quot;underground&quot; affairs happens at night for plenty of reasones. That's said, to have a second sheet for a player is honestly not so much of a deal for any willing ST.... Is like having a player more and you could also consider to use an NPC or a simplified sheet<br /> <br /> The beats can be, with a bit of flexibility, still being addressed to the main character (maybe with the exception of those coming from damages or conditions).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ghouls are not normal humans, they have powers and weaknesses to, so a storyteller would have to study their book too and learn their rules a thing that many are not willing to do, trust me, I've tried everything I could but talking about vampires in multisplat games always brought the kind of awkward silence that tells you everything you need to know about the issue. A shame really because requiem is not masquerade, the writers could have dared more and add a way around this, I mean, vampires aren't even op compared to other splats (if anything they are weaker) so I don't understand this unwillingnes toward making daylight less of an issue, vampires already have a ban and thats fire, I'm not saying to make them daywalkers but at least to make them available during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:29:39-07:00","id":1465550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465532#post1465532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I never understood this wall toward multisplat with vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a CoD thing, this is a players thing.<br /> <br /> First of, a lot of players of other splats are pretty much hostile to Vampire. It has always been the case, since cWoD. It's weird but widespread and I can't offer you an explanation, it just sucks.<br /> <br /> Second, there is this weird sense that sunlight is the ultimate theme of Vampire, a sacred cow that can't be touched. This have to do with cultural loops where movies reinforced the trope again and again and again, with movies that didn't do it having other goals than being dark and edgy, which reinforced the trope by contrast.<br /> <br /> All that starting with 1922's <i>Nosferatu</i>, the very first recorded instance or sunlight destroying vampires. And that just because it was a silent movie and had to be more theatrical to advance the plot with minimal dialogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:48:11-07:00","id":1465551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465532#post1465532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda bummed about it because there is something special about the way vampires play, it would fit neatly into a classic multisplat with a werewolf as the combat monster, a mage as reality warper intellectual and the vampire as the people specialist, CoD prides itself in being more rules friendly toward multi splat gaming and thats true for all them except the vampires, a shame really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves find it harder to access the Shadow during the day and get Essence most easily from seeing a largely nocturnal celestial object. The list of personalized triggers for their uncontrollable rage-state can include &quot;a non-werewolf monster is present.&quot; Staying out of the dimension where they're treated like natives for an extended period of time makes them less effective.<br /> <br /> Changelings have an entire subsplat themed around secrets and the dark. Their otherworld is harder to navigate if you aren't fae. Their sense of what's real is imperiled by realized they've been lied to and having promises broken.<br /> <br /> Prometheans literally make everyone they interact with who isn't a particular subset of monstrous destructively obsessed with them with enough interaction, and this state is contagious.<br /> <br /> Mummies are often running on a timer that goes by quicker when they're off-task, and they're often constrained by geography in terms of their cult and their tomb on top of extended contact with mortals outside their cult being an impetus for demonic incursion.<br /> <br /> People who know a demon as a demon have ready access to information that disintegrates their human lives, and monsters can't pact away parts of their social network that aren't mortal-based.<br /> <br /> Deviants are built to be laser-focused on their Touchstones in frankly unhealthy ways, and their ability to reassign Touchstones is starkly metered even before bringing in the worldwide web of conspiracies they're engaged with.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your group is best suited to convening at night if it's got a vampire in it&quot; is a comparative non-issue \u2014 almost all of the games lean harder into being focused on their own concerns at higher Supernatural Potency ratings, and Vampire in particular gives you more tools to be active during the day at high Humanity and low Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Have a well-equipped Haven to end your night on. Cultivate Resilience. Dress like you don't want your identity discovered. Owe some favors to an Ascendant Dragon if need be. Pursue Disciplines and Devotions to let you telepresence your way around your flesh body being extremely flammable.<br /> <br /> Most people in-setting are going to have more free time and freedom of movement after dark, and vampires work just fine in crossover play with that in mind \u2014 the characters do not inhabit an abstract setting where stuff happens at all hours, considering that the Shadow is largely nocturnal, the Primordial Dream is nocturnal outside of Chambers and the Day, there are entire sections of the Hedge where the sun never rises, Infrastructure is frequently an indoor affair, the Underworld is the Underworld, and monstrous involvement in mortal society means folks like mummies (and, indeed, vampires) can contrive secret passageways around the city that only those in the know or obsessed enough to piece together the architecture would be aware of. Hunter's antagonist book for vampires puts an extensive warren of tunnels underneath a Philadelphia cemetery.<br /> <br /> What kind of games were these STs running where none of this was viable?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465535#post1465535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls are not normal humans, they have powers and weaknesses to, so a storyteller would have to study their book too and learn their rules</div> </div> </div> </div>Their weakness is that they're mortal and their powers run on fuel they can't get themselves. &quot;Their book&quot; is one page of notes and three pages of Merits they can take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465550#post1465550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, there is this weird sense that sunlight is the ultimate theme of Vampire, a sacred cow that can't be touched. This have to do with cultural loops where movies reinforced the trope again and again and again, with movies that didn't do it having other goals than being dark and edgy, which reinforced the trope by contrast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being alienated from your former humanity by having your day-night cycle flipped and taking damage from exposure to something humans do poorly without is more than just &quot;movies did it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the one bane that Kindred powers can't fully mitigate and the primary basis for the All-Night Society. Dracula is not the be-all-end-all of How Vampires Should Be in Requiem, especially not in a game where 1) his name is on the covenant dedicated to overcoming the limits of the Kindred condition and 2) there are vampires that aren't Kindred in the world (including ghuls, who have different concerns from sunlight on their plate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T12:59:11-07:00","id":1465555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465550#post1465550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not a CoD thing, this is a players thing.<br /> <br /> First of, a lot of players of other splats are pretty much hostile to Vampire. It has always been the case, since cWoD. It's weird but widespread and I can't offer you an explanation, it just sucks.<br /> <br /> Second, there is this weird sense that sunlight is the ultimate theme of Vampire, a sacred cow that can't be touched. This have to do with cultural loops where movies reinforced the trope again and again and again, with movies that didn't do it having other goals than being dark and edgy, which reinforced the trope by contrast.<br /> <br /> All that starting with 1922's <i>Nosferatu</i>, the very first recorded instance or sunlight destroying vampires. And that just because it was a silent movie and had to be more theatrical to advance the plot with minimal dialogue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The hostility is not limited to player characters either, during a werewolf game, I asked at the table if we could hunt a vampire, just to introduce a little investigation and social combat in a game that had been so far, the classic balls to the wall werewolf action, the reaction was a stark no no cause none of the players wanted to spend a month worth of sessions building skills that would help with investigations (as for most werewolf games, all of the players except me were built exclusively toward combat, even the elodoth), this hostility goes two ways since most of the vampire players I met don't even want to hear about multisplat, a shame really.<br /> The sunlight thing would be a nice bit of character if it wasn't so debilitating, I mean vampires are the only splat that has 2 major weaknesses while the others only have one (silver for werewolves, cold iron for changelings and human squishiness for mages), I'm not saying to remove it altogether but at least make it so a vampire player wouldn't feel alienated from the rest of the CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T13:21:40-07:00","id":1465558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465551#post1465551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being alienated from your former humanity by having your day-night cycle flipped and taking damage from exposure to something humans do poorly without is more than just &quot;movies did it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the one bane that Kindred powers can't fully mitigate and the primary basis for the All-Night Society. Dracula is not the be-all-end-all of How Vampires Should Be in Requiem, especially not in a game where 1) his name is on the covenant dedicated to overcoming the limits of the Kindred condition and 2) there are vampires that aren't Kindred in the world (including ghuls, who have different concerns from sunlight on their plate).</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula isn't, but apparently <i>Nosferatu</i> is, since no legend or story ever portrayed vampires burning in the sun before it. Not a single one in any part of the world.<br /> <br /> And yet most of them have the night-cycle flipped because as chtonic creatures vampires prefer the night, and one thing that isn't all that uncommon is for them to be weaker under the sun. Not extremely weaker, just robbed of some or all of their preternatural powers.<br /> <br /> Would you walk during the day a lot if it meant saying goodbye to your disciplines and damage resistance for a while? Especially when there are rules for being sleepy during the day already.<br /> <br /> For goodness' sake, I thought vampires were excluded from mankind by becoming <b>frigging predators</b>, not by avoiding sunbaths. Otherwise you would just join the bunch of people that live most through the night anyway for one reason or another. But you can't simply do that not because of the sun, but because <i>there's a thing inside of you seeing them as burgers</i>.<br /> <br /> So sure, it isn't <i>just</i> &quot;movies did it&quot;. It is <i>mostly</i> &quot;movies did it&quot;, with the addition of it being a quaint detail to explore in some stories, a good weakness to explore on others, but seriously nothing worth keeping if you're not going to explore those themes anyway because it is a crossover game and not something focused on the party's vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T13:35:27-07:00","id":1465559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465551#post1465551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves find it harder to access the Shadow during the day and get Essence most easily from seeing a largely nocturnal celestial object. The list of personalized triggers for their uncontrollable rage-state can include &quot;a non-werewolf monster is present.&quot; Staying out of the dimension where they're treated like natives for an extended period of time makes them less effective.<br /> <br /> Changelings have an entire subsplat themed around secrets and the dark. Their otherworld is harder to navigate if you aren't fae. Their sense of what's real is imperiled by realized they've been lied to and having promises broken.<br /> <br /> Prometheans literally make everyone they interact with who isn't a particular subset of monstrous destructively obsessed with them with enough interaction, and this state is contagious.<br /> <br /> Mummies are often running on a timer that goes by quicker when they're off-task, and they're often constrained by geography in terms of their cult and their tomb on top of extended contact with mortals outside their cult being an impetus for demonic incursion.<br /> <br /> People who know a demon as a demon have ready access to information that disintegrates their human lives, and monsters can't pact away parts of their social network that aren't mortal-based.<br /> <br /> Deviants are built to be laser-focused on their Touchstones in frankly unhealthy ways, and their ability to reassign Touchstones is starkly metered even before bringing in the worldwide web of conspiracies they're engaged with.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your group is best suited to convening at night if it's got a vampire in it&quot; is a comparative non-issue \u2014 almost all of the games lean harder into being focused on their own concerns at higher Supernatural Potency ratings, and Vampire in particular gives you more tools to be active during the day at high Humanity and low Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Have a well-equipped Haven to end your night on. Cultivate Resilience. Dress like you don't want your identity discovered. Owe some favors to an Ascendant Dragon if need be. Pursue Disciplines and Devotions to let you telepresence your way around your flesh body being extremely flammable.<br /> <br /> Most people in-setting are going to have more free time and freedom of movement after dark, and vampires work just fine in crossover play with that in mind \u2014 the characters do not inhabit an abstract setting where stuff happens at all hours, considering that the Shadow is largely nocturnal, the Primordial Dream is nocturnal outside of Chambers and the Day, there are entire sections of the Hedge where the sun never rises, Infrastructure is frequently an indoor affair, the Underworld is the Underworld, and monstrous involvement in mortal society means folks like mummies (and, indeed, vampires) can contrive secret passageways around the city that only those in the know or obsessed enough to piece together the architecture would be aware of. Hunter's antagonist book for vampires puts an extensive warren of tunnels underneath a Philadelphia cemetery.<br /> <br /> What kind of games were these STs running where none of this was viable?<br /> <br /> Their weakness is that they're mortal and their powers run on fuel they can't get themselves. &quot;Their book&quot; is one page of notes and three pages of Merits they can take.<br /> <br /> Being alienated from your former humanity by having your day-night cycle flipped and taking damage from exposure to something humans do poorly without is more than just &quot;movies did it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the one bane that Kindred powers can't fully mitigate and the primary basis for the All-Night Society. Dracula is not the be-all-end-all of How Vampires Should Be in Requiem, especially not in a game where 1) his name is on the covenant dedicated to overcoming the limits of the Kindred condition and 2) there are vampires that aren't Kindred in the world (including ghuls, who have different concerns from sunlight on their plate).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference between the other splats and vampires is that they can function in the day without issues while vampires slowly start roasting every time they poke their nose out, that seem like a slightly harder thing to get around compared to the other splats. As for the story tellers, I really have no idea, I've never been a story teller but since most of the games I played tended to be low key and more about smaller, personal events than the high octane stuff that is in the books, I guess that the st didn't want to add secret tunnels and trips to other dimensions (I don't know much about the other splats since I mainly played vampire, werewolf and mage but I honestly don't even know if a vampire could access the shadow in the first place and even if it did, I wouldn't give it an high unlife expectancy either).<br /> Regarding ghouls I must have mistaken the book for something out of the first edition or masquerede where there were entire families of ghouls and all had their quirks, I remember it was a book not just some pages but I might be wrong.<br /> We can discuss about the psychology behind the sunlight weakness all we want but the crux of the matter is that, at least in my experience, multisplat ST tend to avoid vampires and use the inability to be active during the day as the main reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T15:59:48-07:00","id":1465572,"title":"","content":"The more you talk about things, the less it sounds like a problem with the game and more a problem with your group(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T17:06:26-07:00","id":1465577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465558#post1465558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula isn't, but apparently <i>Nosferatu</i> is, since no legend or story ever portrayed vampires burning in the sun before it. Not a single one in any part of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar, having literally read Dracula and watched Nosferatu and written on them for college credit. You will note that this hasn't stopped <i>a whole bunch of other media since</i> from picking it up because it's an evocative visual and a clear restriction that's become practically synonymous with the pop-cultural image of the vampire, which is a more particular thing than the broad umbrella of &quot;vampires&quot; in culture (for which see the entire book of non-Kindred vampires that first gave us the Strix in a modern context).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet most of them have the night-cycle flipped because as chtonic creatures vampires prefer the night, and one thing that isn't all that uncommon is for them to be weaker under the sun. Not extremely weaker, just robbed of some or all of their preternatural powers. </div> </div> </div>\u200bParticularly weak ghosts dissolve in sunlight, and the vast majority of spirits in the Shadow are pinned down and made lethargic by the light of Helios, to say nothing of how the former get dragged down to a cavern-world to get sucked into the walls and the former inhabit a plane where the weather is mostly overcast on account of all the cloud-spirits that never die.<br /> <br /> Kindred are corpses. They can't heal without spending energy they pulled out of alive people. Even without the bloodline specifically built around spreading disease they are plague-carriers by the nature of what they are. They lie all the time to the point where &quot;keeping people from finding out you're a vampire&quot; has a fancy name and major cultural stake in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Brandeis did not get &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunlight_is_the_best_disinfectant\" target=\"_blank\">sunlight is the best disinfectant</a>&quot; <a href=\"https://quoteinvestigator.com/2020/09/22/sunlight/\" target=\"_blank\">from nowhere</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you walk during the day a lot if it meant saying goodbye to your disciplines and damage resistance for a while? Especially when there are rules for being sleepy during the day already. </div> </div> </div>The rules for resisting daysleep are literally the same as the rules for being sleepy for everyone else aside from the timing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For goodness' sake, I thought vampires were excluded from mankind by becoming <b>frigging predators</b>, not by avoiding sunbaths. Otherwise you would just join the bunch of people that live most through the night anyway for one reason or another. But you can't simply do that not because of the sun, but because <i>there's a thing inside of you seeing them as burgers</i>. </div> </div> </div>The effects of going for a long time without being able to see the sun are well-documented and werewolves are right there as a point of comparison for what &quot;becoming a predator&quot; does to your mindset. Vampires are life-drinkers whose constitution doesn't particularly care if they're getting blood by hunting or playing parasite, hence the addiction angle present in their being processing plants for Refined Life-Force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So sure, it isn't <i>just</i> &quot;movies did it&quot;. It is <i>mostly</i> &quot;movies did it&quot;, with the addition of it being a quaint detail to explore in some stories, a good weakness to explore on others, but seriously nothing worth keeping if you're not going to explore those themes anyway because it is a crossover game and not something focused on the party's vampire. </div> </div> </div>Again, much as with Prometheans becoming increasingly hate-magnet-y, werewolves needing increasingly specific food to sustain themselves, changelings being increasingly easy to dissociate from reality, demons being increasingly easily compromised, and all of Mummy's standard package, this is a problem &quot;focused on the party's [splat member]&quot; <i>at higher power-levels</i>.<br /> <br /> A starting vampire character can dress for winter and take no damage at all, or cut that down to <i>one point of lethal damage per ten minutes</i> if for some reason they need to stand around in the middle of the day, but the sorts of Kindred who spontaneously combust under the daystar have been dead for at least half a century or otherwise been leaning hard into being an otherworldly monster whose &quot;other world&quot; is &quot;institutional corruption&quot; and/or &quot;the night.&quot; The gamelines' general trend is that as you rise in power you become <i>more of the kind of monster you are</i>, which usually means having more pressing concerns than facilitating casual cooperation with other sorts of monster.<br /> <br /> Relatively few splats have their drawbacks completely front-loaded, and those that do tend to have unusual relations to their Supernatural Potency and/or Integrity systems, like Sin-Eaters, Deviants, and the Arisen. It's very easy to do a crossover game where everyone has good reason to think everyone else is basically mortal aside from a few particular quirks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T17:51:32-07:00","id":1465579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465572#post1465572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more you talk about things, the less it sounds like a problem with the game and more a problem with your group(s).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been playing for about two years, I'm not gonna pretend I kept count of how many games I played (especially because a lot of them died pretty soon) but unless I've had a really long streak of bad luck, most of the ST's that ran multisplat games didn't want vampires for one reason or the other, I really couldn't care less about vampires and the sun as a concept but if it gets in the way of fun, then I feel it should be adressed, besides, the post is about crazy ideas, whats crazier than suggesting vampires could stand a little more sun in their requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T18:05:14-07:00","id":1465582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will note that this hasn't stopped <i>a whole bunch of other media since</i> from picking it up because it's an evocative visual and a clear restriction that's become practically synonymous with the pop-cultural image of the vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you noticed that this is the definition of &quot;movies did it&quot;?<br /> <br /> Which isn't a bad thing, by the way. At no point I said it is, as I'm not against the trope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which is a more particular thing than the broad umbrella of &quot;vampires&quot; in culture</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet in this same particular thing exceptions abound, to the point that <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DaywalkingVampire\" target=\"_blank\">the Daywalking Vampire is a recognized trope with a huge list of sample works</a>. Most recognize the weakness but either reduce it or create exceptions, but some outright ignore it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred are corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>And corpses don't feed in blood (nor anything else), don't walk and don't burn under the sun. In fact most burials happen during the day and the family sees the coffin being closed under broad daylight.<br /> <br /> Explaining why the weakness makes sense in a fictional world doesn't make it obligatory for the fiction. And indeed it kills the trope of the vampire raising after being buried, that is the origin of their lying in coffins thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brandeis did not get &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunlight_is_the_best_disinfectant\" target=\"_blank\">sunlight is the best disinfectant</a>&quot; <a href=\"https://quoteinvestigator.com/2020/09/22/sunlight/\" target=\"_blank\">from nowhere</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he got it out of earlier philosophers talking about how gaslights helped to reduce crime in London and how sunlight <i>was literally a disinfectant for malaria-infected surfaces</i>, to use it, as he did later, as a metaphor for publicity as a deterrent to crime and corruption.<br /> <br /> It is sure a nice metaphor that makes the weakness more interesting, so what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for resisting daysleep are literally the same as the rules for being sleepy for everyone else aside from the timing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I see no problem with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effects of going for a long time without being able to see the sun are well-documented</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet vampires do not suffer them because it have no bearing on the themes or mechanics of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and werewolves are right there as a point of comparison for what &quot;becoming a predator&quot; does to your mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I should have said vampires are addicted cannibals, not predators.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465577#post1465577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gamelines' general trend is that as you rise in power you become <i>more of the kind of monster you are</i>, which usually means having more pressing concerns than facilitating casual cooperation with other sorts of monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vampire does this by needing more potent Blood. The problem here is that the daylight damage isn't creating concerns, is blocking the character from interacting with the story. Instead of being a thing that adds drama and story hooks, it is just a hard limitation that removes the character from the scene.<br /> <br /> What you're doing is exactly what I said earlier: <b><u>treating a thematic element as a sacred cow</u></b>.<br /> <br /> Absolutely none of this matters in the slightest. Vampires don't exist. This is just a game of telling stories. What matters is the story and the themes it will explore.<br /> <br /> No one here is talking about eliminating the weakness to sunlight or to reduce the damage for normal games. But the mere thought of doing so for specific games enrages you that much.<br /> <br /> Unless the player really wants to do so, I won't force only one PC in the group to have two characters just because of a sacred cow. I won't forbid a player from a splat in a multi-splat game just because of a sacred cow. I won't harm my story idea or the enjoyment of a player just because of a sacred cow. <b><u>If no compromise satisfies me, I'll butcher the cow, it isn't that important</u></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T18:48:49-07:00","id":1465591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465532#post1465532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I never understood this wall toward multisplat with vampires, you would think rules could be bent a little but I assure you that, save that single game I played, most of the storytellers absolutely refused to have vampires in the chronicle and I understand their point of view, not being able to stand sunlight is a pretty big limitation and not something you could work around easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the wall against multisplat with Vampires is mostly coming from the other direction. I don't want anyone playing anything other than Vampires in my Vampire game, both for reasons of tone and balance. On the other hand, if I were running Werewolf and someone wanted to play a Vampire I would be more inclined to allow it (after informing the prospective player that basically all the Werewolf NPCs are going to treat their character with barely contained hostility and contempt). I'd probably also push the player towards being part of the Ordo Dracul so that they could daywalk more easily, and while I wouldn't want to sun weakness to disappear completely, I would be more inclined to fudge it a bit to allow the player to stay involved with the story during the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465532#post1465532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda bummed about it because there is something special about the way vampires play, it would fit neatly into a classic multisplat with a werewolf as the combat monster, a mage as reality warper intellectual and the vampire as the people specialist</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this way of looking at the splats is something a lot more people will find issue with. Comparing the splats like they're different classes immediately sends up warning flags for me. I want to play Vampire, Werewolf, or Mage because the themes of those games appeal to me. When I play Werewolf, I want to feel like a primal hunter who is at home with his pack, and whose whole supernatural existence is like a drug addiction he can't kick that's ruining his mortal life. I may also happen to be better at combat than most Vampires, but that's not really the point.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, while like I said I might be happy to accommodate one player playing another splat I probably wouldn't stretch to two, and certainly not to having three different splats as player characters in the game. While I do love bringing in the other splats as NPCs, I don't feel like the themes of whatever game I'm going for could survive having three different splats represented at the table, and a freeform play-what-you-want game for its own sake is just not something I am very interested in running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T19:06:05-07:00","id":1465592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465582#post1465582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vampire does this by needing more potent Blood. The problem here is that the daylight damage isn't creating concerns, is blocking the character from interacting with the story. Instead of being a thing that adds drama and story hooks, it is just a hard limitation that removes the character from the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: Mummies manage just fine using proxies and have similarly stark limits on their activity cycles, which is another reason I put forward access to the organization rules as something I'd like to see for Requiem 3e, especially given the explicit comparison the text makes of ghouls as parts of their regnants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one here is talking about eliminating the weakness to sunlight or to reduce the damage for normal games. But the mere thought of doing so for specific games enrages you that much. </div> </div> </div>Not enraged, but I <i>will</i> point at the thread title, observe that this discussion exists for a purpose that has nothing to do with normal games, and express my lack of concern for how much bearing an individual game where large timeskips happen with no torpor to hold back the thickening of the blood has on how the base game is built to operate.<br /> <br /> Nobody is talking about a sacred cow. What's being talked about is the prospect of slaughtering your dairy cows so that the surf-and-turf restaurant two cities over can get a package deal on beef with fish. You can put whatever you like on your plate, but your plate is not the farm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T19:41:56-07:00","id":1465595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465591#post1465591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the wall against multisplat with Vampires is mostly coming from the other direction. I don't want anyone playing anything other than Vampires in my Vampire game, both for reasons of tone and balance. On the other hand, if I were running Werewolf and someone wanted to play a Vampire I would be more inclined to allow it (after informing the prospective player that basically all the Werewolf NPCs are going to treat their character with barely contained hostility and contempt). I'd probably also push the player towards being part of the Ordo Dracul so that they could daywalk more easily, and while I wouldn't want to sun weakness to disappear completely, I would be more inclined to fudge it a bit to allow the player to stay involved with the story during the day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like this way of looking at the splats is something a lot more people will find issue with. Comparing the splats like they're different classes immediately sends up warning flags for me. I want to play Vampire, Werewolf, or Mage because the themes of those games appeal to me. When I play Werewolf, I want to feel like a primal hunter who is at home with his pack, and whose whole supernatural existence is like a drug addiction he can't kick that's ruining his mortal life. I may also happen to be better at combat than most Vampires, but that's not really the point.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, while like I said I might be happy to accommodate one player playing another splat I probably wouldn't stretch to two, and certainly not to having three different splats as player characters in the game. While I do love bringing in the other splats as NPCs, I don't feel like the themes of whatever game I'm going for could survive having three different splats represented at the table, and a freeform play-what-you-want game for its own sake is just not something I am very interested in running.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I already wrote before, I'm perfectly aware that the wall is coming from both directions and I still think its a pity because, unlike WoD, CoD was built, among other things, to be more splat firendly a thing that many players and storytellers seem to have an hard time grasping. The various splats are built around a different tone thats true but nothing stops you from building some overlap between them, werewolves and vampires for example, they both hunt prey (werewolves hunts different prey due to their need to hunt, vampires do it for substenance), they both are addicted to it and such addiction is ruining or has already ruined their life (altough vampires tend to have it worse them them imo), the fundamental difference between them is that werewolves have their pack while vampires are solitary creatures and this could be a great theme to explore in a campaign, it would reinforce the werewolf bond with his pack, making it realize that no matter the odds, it will never be alone, while the vampire would have a stark reminder of how lonely its existence is and push it more and more into the downward spiral that will inevitably result in its eternal damnation. This was just a stupid example that came out of my head but someone more experienced could come up with something better because vampires mesh with everything really so saying that the themes don't mesh sounds like a flimsy excuse to me and my example about the 3 splats was from a purely mechanical standpoint so nothing to do with the campaign mood.<br /> Also, nobody said that you should run a campaign with all the splats but if you are willing to run a game with a mage, a changeling and a werewolf and as soon as I tell you that I want to play a vampire you first use the excuse of the sunlight and then you tell me that the splat is too complicated (I'm not kidding, it really happened) then I can only assume that you don't like the splat in particular and should just say so without excuses, nothing wrong with it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T20:31:25-07:00","id":1465596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465592#post1465592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: Mummies manage just fine using proxies</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great <b>option</b>. But while Mummy was built specifically to be played that way, I don't see the point of telling a Vampire player that the only way to take part in a intended crossover game is to either stay weak or use a proxy when no one else does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465592#post1465592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not enraged, but I <i>will</i> point at the thread title</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and someone said they would want an easier option to alleviate the weakness when it comes to crossovers. So what? This is a valid question.<br /> <br /> Let me put it this way:<br /> <br /> <b>I want for 3rd edition Requiem a section dedicated to adjusting the effects of sunlight, with both rules and discussion on their uses, similar to what L5R 4th Edition have for Health calculation.<br /> <br /> And I also want a fair presentation of the option of removing the sunlight weakness entirely, or making it completely lethal.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465592#post1465592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">observe that this discussion exists for a purpose that has nothing to do with normal games</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such a thing as a normal game. The Core book is built to give tools for as many styles of play as possible within the setting. The crossover and the Game of Ages, by the way, are staples that pretty much need space in the core anyway, as they're popular archetypal options that raise more rules concerns tan usual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465592#post1465592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's being talked about is the prospect of slaughtering your dairy cows so that the surf-and-turf restaurant two cities over can get a package deal on beef with fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please enlighten me on just how putting an option in the book will kill the game for everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T22:02:01-07:00","id":1465602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465596#post1465596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great <b>option</b>. But while Mummy was built specifically to be played that way, I don't see the point of telling a Vampire player that the only way to take part in a intended crossover game is to either stay weak or use a proxy when no one else does.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the game that, prior to Mummy, was <i>the game </i>for which &quot;leave stuff to proxies&quot; was a valid and common problem-solving method? The game where you have regular access to an addictive substance and various mind-whammies to get other people to do what you want?<br /> <br /> The line that, way back in the day, was characterized as the Social game to Werewolf's Physical game and Mage's Mental game? The one whose stated check against Awakened power was being able to shift large groups of Sleepers to interfere with Supernal magic, and whose main ability to be a thorn in a werewolf pack's side involved their influence in the mortal sphere vis-a-vis zoning laws and land development and so on?<br /> <br /> You don't see the point of telling a Vampire player to <i>lean into the tools their game gives them</i> to participate in a cooperative effort that takes place outside of their ability to safely participate personally?<br /> <br /> I'll take your word for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no such a thing as a normal game. The Core book is built to give tools for as many styles of play as possible within the setting. The crossover and the Game of Ages, by the way, are staples that pretty much need space in the core anyway, as they're popular archetypal options that raise more rules concerns tan usual. </div> </div> </div>The Vampire: the Requiem corebook exists to give you the tools to play Vampire: the Requiem. You cannot use it on its own to play Werewolf: the Forsaken, Changeling: the Lost, Mage: the Awakening, or the rest. A normal game of Vampire: the Requiem is Vampire: the Requiem and not one of the other Chronicles of Darkness games. The Monster Mash being popular does not make it a reasonable priority for a game specifically about playing vampires dealing with the state of being a vampire.<br /> <br /> Like, my dream for ChroD 3e is that the core rulebook covers as much ground as possible (cults and conspiracies, mortal magics, player ephemera, mysterious places, etc) and the gamelines give separate looks at what a given monster's intrinsic state does to them versus how their social networks mess with that (Being A Vampire versus The All Night Society, solitary mages versus the Consilium and mentor/student bonds, the way Lodges bring a whole lot of Dark Trouble into werewolf society through their spiritual patronage, etc), but breadth of options doesn't change the fact that the base game is the base game first and crossover fuel second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T01:16:06-07:00","id":1465612,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Could we tone down the aggressiveness in this thread? Complaining about the alteration of folklore creatures across the years is not something to get heated over.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T05:24:54-07:00","id":1465624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465602#post1465602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't see the point of telling a Vampire player to <i>lean into the tools their game gives them</i> to participate in a cooperative effort that takes place outside of their ability to safely participate personally?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do see the point of this. I don't see the point of telling them this is the <b><u>only</u></b> right way to play the game in this situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465602#post1465602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vampire: the Requiem corebook exists to give you the tools to play Vampire: the Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. But I don't see where giving more versatility to this particular weakness is not playing Vampire: The Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465602#post1465602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Monster Mash being popular does not make it a reasonable priority</div> </div> </div> </div>And I didn't said it should be a priority. I said it should be a page. Maybe a side box, even.<br /> <br /> Why is that so unreasonable?<br /> <br /> By the way, I don't think a quick guide on how to tune the sunlight weakness to adapt to the style of your chronicle would be good for crossovers. I think it would be great for Vampire: The Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T05:42:25-07:00","id":1465627,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure there are suggestions in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle for handling this exact issue of allowing Vampires to operate during the day in a multi-splat chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:03:46-07:00","id":1465628,"title":"","content":"From someone who only skimmed the recent arguments about sunlight: I think\u2019s it\u2019s something closer to werewolves\u2019 dietary restrictions and hunting periods (as opposed to, say, silver and Rage), and mages\u2019 Long-Term Nimbus (as opposed to, say, Paradox). It\u2019s a deliberately placed thematic and dramatic restriction\u2026 that I feel can be waived for practical purposes in running a game, without necessarily excising it, or even dampening it. And that is all.<br /> <br /> Of course, a sidebar or two saying that explicitly would be of help. And of course the addition of general Organization rules to get around sunlight rules without trivializing it, like how Shadow Names allow mages to get around Nimbus rules without ignoring it (and empowering the mage while it\u2019s at it too!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465627#post1465627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure there are suggestions in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle for handling this exact issue of allowing Vampires to operate during the day in a multi-splat chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give us a tiny peek within reasonable bounds, if possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 10-28-2021, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:15:51-07:00","id":1465629,"title":"","content":"PDF at home. zee PaTrick at work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T12:17:25-07:00","id":1465677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465628#post1465628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From someone who only skimmed the recent arguments about sunlight: I think\u2019s it\u2019s something closer to werewolves\u2019 dietary restrictions and hunting periods (as opposed to, say, silver and Rage), and mages\u2019 Long-Term Nimbus (as opposed to, say, Paradox). It\u2019s a deliberately placed thematic and dramatic restriction\u2026 that I feel can be waived for practical purposes in running a game, without necessarily excising it, or even dampening it. And that is all.<br /> <br /> Of course, a sidebar or two saying that explicitly would be of help. And of course the addition of general Organization rules to get around sunlight rules without trivializing it, like how Shadow Names allow mages to get around Nimbus rules without ignoring it (and empowering the mage while it\u2019s at it too!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Could you give us a tiny peek within reasonable bounds, if possible?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just bought the contagion chronicles (its on sale on drivethru for anyone who cares), from what I've read so far there is only a merit that lets you ignore a splat's bane (all the splats) for a scene in exchange of a permanent dot of lethal damage, doesn't exactly feel like a workable fix to me. The rest of the suggestions I read so far basically ammount to &quot;do what you want&quot; when it comes to splat weaknesses but I'm speed reading the thing so I most likely got something wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T12:48:05-07:00","id":1465681,"title":"","content":"Did you get the Player's Guide as well? It goes deeper into splat on splat interactions. I haven't read it since the backer pdf dropped but I remember there being suggestions on vampires in daylight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T12:50:50-07:00","id":1465682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465681#post1465681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you get the Player's Guide as well? It goes deeper into splat on splat interactions. I haven't read it since the backer pdf dropped but I remember there being suggestions on vampires in daylight</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just bought it too, gonna start reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T12:59:20-07:00","id":1465683,"title":"","content":"Just read it, it basically says what I suggested in my other posts, have sunlight mess with the disciplines instead of healt box, it still doesn't make it a rule, just a suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:02:35-07:00","id":1465684,"title":"","content":"But its a valid in a book suggestion that you can take to your ST as an in the book suggestion for going forward","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:17:31-07:00","id":1465687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465684#post1465684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But its a valid in a book suggestion that you can take to your ST as an in the book suggestion for going forward</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its something I guess, had it made into a paragraph or even a box in an eventual 3ed would make it easier since I'm pretty sure the st couldn't just tell me to shove it and pick another splat if it were written in the manual or at least they would have to be honest and just say they don't like the splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:46:37-07:00","id":1465690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465683#post1465683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just read it, it basically says what I suggested in my other posts, have sunlight mess with the disciplines instead of healt box, it still doesn't make it a rule, just a suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a rule in the sense of changing the core rule instead of giving an alternative for the ST to apply, then you really won't have a rule. But I think this is already a very good idea to put in a sidebox in the 3rd core.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think your ST have already made it pretty clear they just don't like the splat and prefer to be a jerk about it instead of going forward about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:51:45-07:00","id":1465691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465690#post1465690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a rule in the sense of changing the core rule instead of giving an alternative for the ST to apply, then you really won't have a rule. But I think this is already a very good idea to put in a sidebox in the 3rd core.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think your ST have already made it pretty clear they just don't like the splat and prefer to be a jerk about it instead of going forward about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course I don't want them to change the rule, just have it write it in a box that the sunlight thing could be worked around instead of being insormountable and as far the ST I wasn't speaking of anyone in particular, just the basic gist I got from most of the multi splat games I played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T14:04:55-07:00","id":1465693,"title":"","content":"So, for the sake of this bit of the discussion, it'd be simple enough to make the hypothetical variant rule into a basic Bane that works like the others in place of damage: &quot;When in direct sunlight, the vampire's rolls to activate Disciplines are capped by her Humanity.&quot; Easy, short, scales like most other banes, creates interesting scenarios where neonates want to shut down an elder and work out a way to bait him into direct sunlight where they have the advantage.<br /> <br /> As for things I'd like to see? More ghoul stuff (particularly giving core-based incentive to keep mandragora), a little space for Threnodies in the core, maybe a little exploration of what exactly elders metamorphose into if all those little hints in the core carry over (Thousand Years of Night, while an interesting enough book, diiidn't really do it for me there). Also, a few examples of one-off, seemingly-fluke ways the Blood can contaminate living things, some more subtle and some more overt, to get the creative juices going - the Chronicles setting is all about weirdness after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T14:35:49-07:00","id":1465698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465693#post1465693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for the sake of this bit of the discussion, it'd be simple enough to make the hypothetical variant rule into a basic Bane that works like the others in place of damage: &quot;When in direct sunlight, the vampire's rolls to activate Disciplines are capped by her Humanity.&quot; Easy, short, scales like most other banes, creates interesting scenarios where neonates want to shut down an elder and work out a way to bait him into direct sunlight where they have the advantage.<br /> <br /> As for things I'd like to see? More ghoul stuff (particularly giving core-based incentive to keep mandragora), a little space for Threnodies in the core, maybe a little exploration of what exactly elders metamorphose into if all those little hints in the core carry over (Thousand Years of Night, while an interesting enough book, diiidn't really do it for me there). Also, a few examples of one-off, seemingly-fluke ways the Blood can contaminate living things, some more subtle and some more overt, to get the creative juices going - the Chronicles setting is all about weirdness after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this, personally I would have discipline roles capped by blood potency (the more powerfull you are, the better you are at using your disciplines in stressful conditions, like in the sunlight) while using humanity to determine the ammount of extra blood you would spend (in daylight everything would cost more blood) with each discipline use and when regenerating (lower humanity would bring something like 4x the normal use depending on the level), have also a draining effect on blood where you lose x ammount of blood points (again capped by humanity) for every 10 minutes you spend in direct sunlight and as soon you run out, you start taking aggravated damage. Its slightly more convulted but I still think it could be worked in the lore and still keep vampires to nightime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-28-2021, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:07:34-07:00","id":1465699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465698#post1465698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, personally I would have discipline roles capped by blood potency (the more powerfull you are, the better you are at using your disciplines in stressful conditions, like in the sunlight) while using humanity to determine the ammount of extra blood you would spend (in daylight everything would cost more blood) with each discipline use and when regenerating (lower humanity would bring something like 4x the normal use depending on the level), have also a draining effect on blood where you lose x ammount of blood points (again capped by humanity) for every 10 minutes you spend in direct sunlight and as soon you run out, you start taking aggravated damage. Its slightly more convulted but I still think it could be worked in the lore and still keep vampires to nightime.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need much to keep vampires to night time. As long as there's <i>any</i> downside to it, they'll switch. Make them drowsy with sleep during day, all day, and no one will want to be out of bed with the sun out no matter how much they can.<br /> <br /> But I think putting too much things on Humanity is a bad idea. This will make high Humanity a too powerful asset and change the dynamics around it. If the difference in power of high and low Humanity vampires is too big, then keeping Humanity high becomes far more of a concern and a focus for Kindred.<br /> <br /> It isn't necessarily a bad thing for every story, but you'll have an All Night Society far more devoted to keeping high Humanity, with Kindred reunions being populated by humans in the know just for socialization in a positive environment, well paid blood donors being a feature, support groups for old vampires with living specialists in archaeological psychology and Soldier-type PTSD, and Dominate would be deemed a liability, not an asset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:25:05-07:00","id":1465701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465699#post1465699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need much to keep vampires to night time. As long as there's <i>any</i> downside to it, they'll switch. Make them drowsy with sleep during day, all day, and no one will want to be out of bed with the sun out no matter how much they can.<br /> <br /> But I think putting too much things on Humanity is a bad idea. This will make high Humanity a too powerful asset and change the dynamics around it. If the difference in power of high and low Humanity vampires is too big, then keeping Humanity high becomes far more of a concern and a focus for Kindred.<br /> <br /> It isn't necessarily a bad thing for every story, but you'll have an All Night Society far more devoted to keeping high Humanity, with Kindred reunions being populated by humans in the know just for socialization in a positive environment, well paid blood donors being a feature, support groups for old vampires with living specialists in archaeological psychology and Soldier-type PTSD, and Dominate would be deemed a liability, not an asset.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea to focus on humanity is to further differentiate neonates from elders, neonates are still new to the whole undead thing, they still think and act following a pattern that mimics their old life, elders meanwhile had more time to adapt and become powerful but in the process lost a lot of what made them human therefore moving away from the sun and moving closer to the all night society. I don't think this would make humanity such an asset to be honest, high humanity characters wouldn't be as powerfull as a 300 year old elder, hell, blood potency could actually be capped by humanity, at 7 humanity BP would be capped at 3 and as soon as humanity drops the cap on BP get higher, this would also play into the role since elders are described as being completely alien to normal human norms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:39:35-07:00","id":1465703,"title":"","content":"I think we're starting to demonstrate why &quot;bit more convoluted,&quot; easily turns into a lot more convoluted and why these sorts of things get scrapped (at least from core books).<br /> <br /> Wanted a quick easy optional rule for vampires to access daylight activities in the core book is a compelling thing for a 3e of VtR.<br /> <br /> When we're getting to the point of trying to hard code in generalities, we're starting to get away from VtR 3e and just into a different vampire game. High Humanity elders are a thing in the game, even if extremely rare because few vampires want to dedicate themselves to what it takes to maintain Humanity that high for that long. Coupling Humanity and Blood Potency starts to have all sorts of knock on effects throughout the system. Ironing out all of that is getting a bit beyond &quot;new edition&quot; territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:53:50-07:00","id":1465706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465701#post1465701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea to focus on humanity is to further differentiate neonates from elders, neonates are still new to the whole undead thing, they still think and act following a pattern that mimics their old life, elders meanwhile had more time to adapt and become powerful but in the process lost a lot of what made them human therefore moving away from the sun and moving closer to the all night society. I don't think this would make humanity such an asset to be honest, high humanity characters wouldn't be as powerfull as a 300 year old elder, hell, blood potency could actually be capped by humanity, at 7 humanity BP would be capped at 3 and as soon as humanity drops the cap on BP get higher, this would also play into the role since elders are described as being completely alien to normal human norms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, vampires are natural competitors. Everything they do, they weigh in how much of an advantage it is against their competitors, even if circumstantial and especially if this is an exploitable circumstance.<br /> <br /> If the difference between High and Low Humanity during the day is too big, they'll evaluate if any benefit from loosing Humanity is actually worth it in this competitive environment.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always send your Ghouls against you opponents or to do your bidding during the day, but as they say, if wan something well done, do it yourself. If you're caught unguarded or have to flee, this is also something to consider.<br /> <br /> Already Humanity is a concern. Having it high is beneficial and most Kindred will at least sometimes weigh the benefits of keeping it or not. The more weight you give it, the more they'll lean towards maintaining it.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I really don't like the idea of making it that hard a rule about how much Humanity you can keep at each BP level. This seems just limiting on character concepts, and nothing anyone else asked for just to make high Humanity vampires more playable at day time (and keep them at low BP).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:54:08-07:00","id":1465707,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pretty much what Heavy Arms said - it's waaay too easy to overcomplicate things, and Chronicles... isn't the <i>simplest</i> system in the industry what with the subsystems for combat and research and chases and the like, but it's certainly less crunchy than many and I think that's part of the appeal. Plus, there's something fun about the idea of an ooold vampire who's hellbent on keeping in touch with How The Mortals Do Things even after all this time that capping Humanity via Blood Potency would kinda ruin.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'd actually prefer the sunlight damage thing get streamlined a little too, the current &quot;x damage at y intervals where one variable is determined by Humanity and the other by Blood Potency&quot; thing is just<i> slightly </i>weird and is one of the few base mechanics I still haven't managed to half-memorize. Buuut it's hard to do that without making it too punishing or too lenient so I get why the 2e team went with what they did, and I certainly prefer it to &quot;dead in seconds no matter what&quot; like 1e more-or-less was by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 10-28-2021, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T15:55:57-07:00","id":1465708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465703#post1465703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're starting to demonstrate why &quot;bit more convoluted,&quot; easily turns into a lot more convoluted and why these sorts of things get scrapped (at least from core books).<br /> <br /> Wanted a quick easy optional rule for vampires to access daylight activities in the core book is a compelling thing for a 3e of VtR.<br /> <br /> When we're getting to the point of trying to hard code in generalities, we're starting to get away from VtR 3e and just into a different vampire game. High Humanity elders are a thing in the game, even if extremely rare because few vampires want to dedicate themselves to what it takes to maintain Humanity that high for that long. Coupling Humanity and Blood Potency starts to have all sorts of knock on effects throughout the system. Ironing out all of that is getting a bit beyond &quot;new edition&quot; territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not like the changes between 1ed and 2ed were little things either, a new edition could mean anything not just a few fixes here and there, still, the title of the post is about crazy ideas, things that most likely won't be added in an eventual 3ed (if there will be one in the first place) so suggesting a little bit of radical change is not going to derail the thread. Anyway my point stand, however they want to do it, shall a 3ed ever come out, I would like a way to get around the sun problem at least for the purpose of multisplat games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:03:38-07:00","id":1465709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465706#post1465706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, vampires are natural competitors. Everything they do, they weigh in how much of an advantage it is against their competitors, even if circumstantial and especially if this is an exploitable circumstance.<br /> <br /> If the difference between High and Low Humanity during the day is too big, they'll evaluate if any benefit from loosing Humanity is actually worth it in this competitive environment.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always send your Ghouls against you opponents or to do your bidding during the day, but as they say, if wan something well done, do it yourself. If you're caught unguarded or have to flee, this is also something to consider.<br /> <br /> Already Humanity is a concern. Having it high is beneficial and most Kindred will at least sometimes weigh the benefits of keeping it or not. The more weight you give it, the more they'll lean towards maintaining it.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I really don't like the idea of making it that hard a rule about how much Humanity you can keep at each BP level. This seems just limiting on character concepts, and nothing anyone else asked for just to make high Humanity vampires more playable at day time (and keep them at low BP).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like I wrote above, the crux of the matter was to get a way to act during daytime in an eventual 3ed, however they want to do it, I don't care, the other things I wrote was just my immagination running wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:08:52-07:00","id":1465711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465707#post1465707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the current &quot;x damage at y intervals where one variable is determined by Humanity and the other by Blood Potency&quot; thing</div> </div> </div> </div>As weird as it is, it is already simple to look for in a table and note down for a char, as it won't change that frequently. More importantly, it gives you two dials to work with.<br /> <br /> The reason I mentioned L5R earlier is because Health in there have exactly this proposal for a sidebox. In it your Health is defined as 2\u00d7Earth at each penalty class by default, but a sidebox explains what is expected to happen at a game with this amount and then how to adjust it to your preference, discussing how the game behaves when you change it to \u00d73, \u00d74 or \u00d75. It is a design dial, and the sidebox just straight out teaches the ST how to change the dial to reap an effect.<br /> <br /> So that's basically all we need. What's the effect of messing around with the dials? What are the designer notes about different settings? They do have this information because they have it from the very design process, just share it with the STs.<br /> <br /> One addition I think is worth to make is to offer the two extreme settings: no damage and insta-death. Limits on Disciplines are an option when you have no damage. The most important thing, though, is to discuss as designers what are the effects on the game for using any particular setting on the dials. It is crunch-light, but the discussion is the important part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:11:20-07:00","id":1465712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465711#post1465711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As weird as it is, it is already simple to look for in a table and note down for a char, as it won't change that frequently. More importantly, it gives you two dials to work with.<br /> <br /> The reason I mentioned L5R earlier is because Health in there have exactly this proposal for a sidebox. In it your Health is defined as 2\u00d7Earth at each penalty class by default, but a sidebox explains what is expected to happen at a game with this amount and then how to adjust it to your preference, discussing how the game behaves when you change it to \u00d73, \u00d74 or \u00d75. It is a design dial, and the sidebox just straight out teaches the ST how to change the dial to reap an effect.<br /> <br /> So that's basically all we need. What's the effect of messing around with the dials? What are the designer notes about different settings? They do have this information because they have it from the very design process, just share it with the STs.<br /> <br /> One addition I think is worth to make is to offer the two extreme settings: no damage and insta-death. Limits on Disciplines are an option when you have no damage. The most important thing, though, is to discuss as designers what are the effects on the game for using any particular setting on the dials. It is crunch-light, but the discussion is the important part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How could it work lore wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:42:12-07:00","id":1465723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465712#post1465712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could it work lore wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>It changes nothing. Health levels and X damage per Y time don't exist lore-wise, they're abstractions. And the dial isn't a character thing, it is a chronicle thing. Whatever your setting is, it is how things work in your chronicle, and how they always have worked, unless you specifically want to make it otherwise.<br /> <br /> There are minor details, sure, and the discussion in the box/page is also about this, but the implementation is really simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:16:51-07:00","id":1465730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465723#post1465723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It changes nothing. Health levels and X damage per Y time don't exist lore-wise, they're abstractions. And the dial isn't a character thing, it is a chronicle thing. Whatever your setting is, it is how things work in your chronicle, and how they always have worked, unless you specifically want to make it otherwise.<br /> <br /> There are minor details, sure, and the discussion in the box/page is also about this, but the implementation is really simple.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The core book makes the sun kinda of a big deal, I mean what you say make sense mechanically but when you have the ordo dracul developing an entire coil around fixing vampires tan problem, you would need something more than &quot;lets just pretend sun is not a problem for this chronicle&quot;, its one of the reason why I think that the solution proposed in the contagion guide is little more than an half assed fix. It doesn't have to be anything to deep, something along the line &quot;not all vampires are affected from the sun in the same way&quot;, just a little lip service to give it a little more feasibily and constistency with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:26:05-07:00","id":1465735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465730#post1465730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book makes the sun kinda of a big deal, I mean what you say make sense mechanically but when you have the ordo dracul developing an entire coil around fixing vampires tan problem, you would need something more than &quot;lets just pretend sun is not a problem for this chronicle&quot;, its one of the reason why I think that the solution proposed in the contagion guide is little more than an half assed fix. It doesn't have to be anything to deep, something along the line &quot;not all vampires are affected from the sun in the same way&quot;, just a little lip service to give it a little more feasibily and constistency with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any level of weakness is a big deal and worth the investment of a Coil, as long as the effects of the Coil move along with the rule. Saying that some vampires don't work the same way may be more damaging to consistency than assuming for a chronicle that the rules are X and have always been X.<br /> <br /> By the way, consistency is also maintained in the sense that as long as a chronicle follows internal consistency it is considered a Shard as per the supplement Mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T00:06:29-07:00","id":1465743,"title":"","content":"The problem with making high Humanity too crucial is that it'll make Cru\u00e0c blood sorcery even less appealing, since just learning about it forever cap your Humanity level. So you'd either have to give Cru\u00e0c users broken powers or make the Circle the least interesting of the Covenants mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T02:41:18-07:00","id":1465745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465735#post1465735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any level of weakness is a big deal and worth the investment of a Coil, as long as the effects of the Coil move along with the rule. Saying that some vampires don't work the same way may be more damaging to consistency than assuming for a chronicle that the rules are X and have always been X.<br /> <br /> By the way, consistency is also maintained in the sense that as long as a chronicle follows internal consistency it is considered a Shard as per the supplement Mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't read mirrors, what is some sort alternate reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T02:48:41-07:00","id":1465746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465743#post1465743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with making high Humanity too crucial is that it'll make Cru\u00e0c blood sorcery even less appealing, since just learning about it forever cap your Humanity level. So you'd either have to give Cru\u00e0c users broken powers or make the Circle the least interesting of the Covenants mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that would fit with the general theme of the covenants, by delving deeper into your beastial nature you are effectively abandoning you humanity, I still think that having your humanity drop in favor of power would be a good addition for the general mood of the splat, power at a price, your beast compels you to give in tempting you with uninmaginable power yet you still try to cling to your humanity, conscious of the fact that there is a steep price to pay. The system would basically need a total rework I know but as I wrote before, its note like the changes between first and second edition were marginal either. Btw, are there any talk at all about a 3rd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T07:34:43-07:00","id":1465767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465746#post1465746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, are there any talk at all about a 3rd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pacing being what it's been, I think we're at least two years away from hearing anything, what with all the stuff from the current edition still in the pipeline; Mummy 1e coming out so close to the GMC Rules Update was an outlier that's not likely to be repeated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:00:11-07:00","id":1465770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465767#post1465767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pacing being what it's been, I think we're at least two years away from hearing anything, what with all the stuff from the current edition still in the pipeline; Mummy 1e coming out so close to the GMC Rules Update was an outlier that's not likely to be repeated.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the reason that happened was that Mummy was originally supposed to be the first 2nd Edition game, so outlier of outliers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:24:49-07:00","id":1465774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465745#post1465745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read mirrors, what is some sort alternate reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>It basically made canon that alternate realities exist in an infinite number and that is the official state of things in CoD.<br /> <br /> One of the goals was precisely to justify STs making houserules and stuff to their heart's content. The other was to open the way to 2nd edition, so any inconsistency with 1st ed setting is due to multiverse. Finally to empower STs and writers to make even more alterations when they feel like.<br /> <br /> An interesting book. Gonzo as hell, but interesting nonetheless. It added a lot of new considerations and optional rules. It also made an universe where CoD is a Comics universe and every Z-splat is actually a single super hero/villain character. Gonzo as hell.<br /> <br /> But there are other, down-to-earth aspects and in general it is a good book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:31:42-07:00","id":1465775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465767#post1465767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pacing being what it's been, I think we're at least two years away from hearing anything, what with all the stuff from the current edition still in the pipeline; Mummy 1e coming out so close to the GMC Rules Update was an outlier that's not likely to be repeated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What new stuff is supposed to come out? I read about a ghost hunter book for human characters but I don't know anything about other pubblications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:48:38-07:00","id":1465780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465775#post1465775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What new stuff is supposed to come out? I read about a ghost hunter book for human characters but I don't know anything about other pubblications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Hunter is probably the World supplement, not Chronicles.<br /> <br /> THe current new stuff is....it occurs to me I haven't look at the development list in a while, hold on.<br /> <br /> EDIT: so the current list, not including story/story collections, pre-made characters, or currently unannounced projects, includes:<br /> <br /> The Tome of the Pentacle<br /> The Hedge<br /> Contagion Chronicle: Global Outbreaks<br /> The Book of Lasting Death<br /> The Clade Companion<br /> Kith and Kin<br /> The Devoted Companion<br /> Tending the Flame<br /> <br /> Considering this list of follow-ups from kickstarters used to be three times the size, that fact it's this small is actually encouraging, because with only Tending being in the Outline phase and the rest somewhere along the line, we're getting around to a point where the freelancers interested in CHronicles can probably start getting in a lot of pitches with the next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-29-2021, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T09:01:36-07:00","id":1465782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465774#post1465774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It basically made canon that alternate realities exist in an infinite number and that is the official state of things in CoD.<br /> <br /> One of the goals was precisely to justify STs making houserules and stuff to their heart's content. The other was to open the way to 2nd edition, so any inconsistency with 1st ed setting is due to multiverse. Finally to empower STs and writers to make even more alterations when they feel like.<br /> <br /> An interesting book. Gonzo as hell, but interesting nonetheless. It added a lot of new considerations and optional rules. It also made an universe where CoD is a Comics universe and every Z-splat is actually a single super hero/villain character. Gonzo as hell.<br /> <br /> But there are other, down-to-earth aspects and in general it is a good book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will have to read this one, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T10:43:59-07:00","id":1465788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465767#post1465767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pacing being what it's been, I think we're at least two years away from hearing anything, what with all the stuff from the current edition still in the pipeline; Mummy 1e coming out so close to the GMC Rules Update was an outlier that's not likely to be repeated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we actually need a third edition? For Requiem specifically I don't see any problems with the core system that would require a rules update. There are still lots of things I would like to see expanded upon (blood sorcery and bloodlines), including several of the suggestions in this thread (more clans, variations on the standard kindred template such as sun-resistant vampires, etc.) but those could all be handled through supplements.<br /> <br /> My only problems with the core book are mostly from an editing standpoint, e.g. I find it criminal that so much space was given over to reprinting the core rules, but then certain elements like all-out attacks were still ommitted, and it would be nice to get an FAQ to resolve inconsistencies between the wording of 2e's core rules from one gameline to another, but neither of those require a whole new edition of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:32:25-07:00","id":1465807,"title":"","content":"Well, the point of the thread is idle speculation about a third edition; not its necessity.<br /> <br /> I think a 2.5 sort of deal could be healthy, as I don't think the 2e basics need any major change (or at least not any that wouldn't involve some major changes outside of the game line like Paradox selling the CofD to OPP and OPP making a 3e in Storypath for legal reasons). But I'd love to see a revised 2.5e core book, and at least Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Demon, and Beast all get &quot;slim&quot; 2.5e books that don't reprint the main rules. Ideally all of the 2e base material would stay compatible, but just better integration of things and more consistency.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:58:09-07:00","id":1465811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465807#post1465807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the point of the thread is idle speculation about a third edition; not its necessity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we do kind have a necessity on regards to Vampire and Demon for reasons already discussed: they're too marked by being released during the edition transition. But a 2.5 kind of deal would be more than enough, or just an &quot;update guide&quot; for people that already have the books.<br /> <br /> But indeed this is more a space to throw wild ideas than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:08:05-07:00","id":1465814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465780#post1465780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Hunter is probably the World supplement, not Chronicles.<br /> <br /> THe current new stuff is....it occurs to me I haven't look at the development list in a while, hold on.<br /> <br /> EDIT: so the current list, not including story/story collections, pre-made characters, or currently unannounced projects, includes:<br /> <br /> The Tome of the Pentacle<br /> The Hedge<br /> Contagion Chronicle: Global Outbreaks<br /> The Book of Lasting Death<br /> The Clade Companion<br /> Kith and Kin<br /> The Devoted Companion<br /> Tending the Flame<br /> <br /> Considering this list of follow-ups from kickstarters used to be three times the size, that fact it's this small is actually encouraging, because with only Tending being in the Outline phase and the rest somewhere along the line, we're getting around to a point where the freelancers interested in CHronicles can probably start getting in a lot of pitches with the next year.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, thats not a lot to be honest, maybe work on new editions isn't so far along the road...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],