bcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465820#post1465820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, before it used to be a major clog in the sink of stuff that needed to get finished up. While this still represents a hefty bit of work, it's a lot more manageable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not a writer but that doesn't seem like an impossible ammount of work, depending of how many writers were available, I think those could be all published in a year or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:37:28-07:00","id":1465832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465824#post1465824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not a writer but that doesn't seem like an impossible ammount of work, depending of how many writers were available, I think those could be all published in a year or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Writers, developers, artists, possibly lay out artists (if it's nto all getting filtered through the same one guy) all working as contract freelancers on a non-living wage, which means schedules must account that the workforce is also able to do the things that make them the money they need to keep the lights on. It's not <i>that</i> easy peasy.<br /> <br /> But definitely better than it used to be!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:49:44-07:00","id":1465833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465832#post1465832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. Writers, developers, artists, possibly lay out artists (if it's nto all getting filtered through the same one guy) all working as contract freelancers on a non-living wage, which means schedules must account that the workforce is also able to do the things that make them the money they need to keep the lights on. It's not <i>that</i> easy peasy.<br /> <br /> But definitely better than it used to be!</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I get shitty wages and gig economy and I'm speaking out of ignorance on the subject but if publishers are similar to some of the companies I worked for, they will find a way to get it done soner rather than later.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:54:26-07:00","id":1465834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465833#post1465833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I get shitty wages and gig economy and I'm speaking out of ignorance on the subject but if publishers are similar to some of the companies I worked for, they will find a way to get it done soner rather than later.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, Onyx Path isn't a slave driver company, and instead gets things done at a pace that works for more people than not. It pays that after a decade, Onyx Path has earned the trust and patience of it's core audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:57:55-07:00","id":1465836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465834#post1465834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully, Onyx Path isn't a slave driver company, and instead gets things done at a pace that works for more people than not. It pays that after a decade, Onyx Path has earned the trust and patience of it's core audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that I don't know much about the company, good for them if thats the case, one more reason to support them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T03:25:27-07:00","id":1465879,"title":"","content":"For 3ED, I'd want a corebook design similar to 1ED where you get enough information about covenants/factions from the corebook without having to rely on information in previous/out-of-date iterations of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T03:31:12-07:00","id":1465881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465834#post1465834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully, Onyx Path isn't a slave driver company, and instead gets things done at a pace that works for more people than not. It pays that after a decade, Onyx Path has earned the trust and patience of it's core audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I am curious: how did you come the conclusion that OPP has earned the patience of its core audience?<br /> <br /> My read of the core audience is that it is more than a little dissatisfied with the pace of new supplments for a fair bit of its gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T04:07:41-07:00","id":1465884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465767#post1465767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pacing being what it's been, I think we're at least two years away from hearing anything, what with all the stuff from the current edition still in the pipeline; Mummy 1e coming out so close to the GMC Rules Update was an outlier that's not likely to be repeated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't expect anything this side of 2025 !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T04:22:00-07:00","id":1465885,"title":"","content":"&quot;Is gameline X dead/dying&quot; isn't a particularly rare question/topic of discussion. With OPP's inability to produce dedicated books for more than a few of the literal dozen CofD games at a time, and at a glacial pace for the games OPP is actively focusing on, it's no wonder that a lot of core fans (including some who actively participate here and/or the official Discord) have such doubts.<br /> That list includes books for Mage, Changeling, bluebook CofD, Deviant, Mummy, and Hunter, totalling half of the games. It does not include books for Vampire, Werewolf, Promethean, Geist, Demon, or Beast. For all we know, neither of those will get another dedicated book. Especially Vampire's future look grim (even though Spilled Blood is one of the more recent books) since material by alumni writers that could've been compiled to a full book has been released on the STV instead. And even if we do get more books for them as early as next year (doubtful, considering they haven't even been announced yet), that means there would've been a four year gap between books for Promethean, Demon and Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T04:57:58-07:00","id":1465886,"title":"","content":"Well, Demon at least was supposed to a smaller game-line, as far as I remember, right ? So it's bothersome but not too bad if they don't add a large slew of books for them. Vampire's been the flasgship of both WoD and CoD and while it seems CoD is on the second division now clearly, with Paradox focusing back on V5 and Masquarade, I'd love something more for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T08:23:20-07:00","id":1465899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465881#post1465881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I am curious: how did you come the conclusion that OPP has earned the patience of its core audience?<br /> <br /> My read of the core audience is that it is more than a little dissatisfied with the pace of new supplments for a fair bit of its gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general fact they're still waiting at all, and that OPP consistently hits their goals for projects (and, relatedly, has stayed consistent with what those goals look like with their projects). If a decade's worth of taking their time was going to actually be a turn off for people, we'd've seen it by now.<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt that, the majority of the time this topic comes up, there is reliably multiple responses explaining the logic for OPP and expressing support and appreciation for the mentality.<br /> <br /> The noise is not the sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-30-2021, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T10:17:08-07:00","id":1465913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1465881#post1465881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I am curious: how did you come the conclusion that OPP has earned the patience of its core audience?<br /> <br /> My read of the core audience is that it is more than a little dissatisfied with the pace of new supplments for a fair bit of its gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's also the fact that the response for Mummy and Deviant was positive from several parts of the internet that I tend to look at outside of this forum.<br /> <br /> Its also helped by the fact that there are several new fans coming in from time to time enjoying on discord.<br /> <br /> And that's just chronicles with exalted and scion going on with a consistent fanbase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 10-30-2021, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T05:44:30-08:00","id":1469089,"title":"","content":"I'd like an eventual 3d edition of Requiem to be more ST-beginner friendly.<br /> <br /> This is a more general consideration that applies to other gamelines as well. You have a Storytelling chapter with all kinds of advices on how to handle specific themes and scenes and questions to ask players etc., and yet I have still no clue on how to run a Requiem chronicle.<br /> <br /> By reading the book I think an aspiring ST should have an idea of how Requiem stories may look like.<br /> If I'm about to run a D&amp;D for the first time, I have a good idea of what a typical adventure is supposed to be, and I know exactly where to start: make a dungeon, fill it with monsters, put some magic loot, end with a boss fight, done. Of course, this is useful as a starting point: as the DM grows more experienced and confident, stories will probably deviate more from the standard dungeon-crawl.<br /> At least in 1st Edition you had some suggestions on the types of conflicts you could focus on, some examples of story hooks, chronicle ideas etc. That's something I find lacking in 2E.<br /> You might say that CofD gamelines tend to have a more sandbox approach: in that case, the book should provide ST advices and tools like Apocalypse World does. <br /> <br /> Another thing that would need to change in 3d ed: less Strix.<br /> Yes, they're a cool addition. But come on.<br /> Too many Strixes.<br /> There is a staggering 19, NINETEEN different Strix NPCs, and not even a SINGLE sample Ghoul or Kindred NPC.<br /> <br /> So I guess a bit more variety and wider range of ready-made stuff for beginner STs would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T05:52:56-08:00","id":1469165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469089#post1469089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like an eventual 3d edition of Requiem to be more ST-beginner friendly.<br /> <br /> This is a more general consideration that applies to other gamelines as well. You have a Storytelling chapter with all kinds of advices on how to handle specific themes and scenes and questions to ask players etc., and yet I have still no clue on how to run a Requiem chronicle.<br /> <br /> By reading the book I think an aspiring ST should have an idea of how Requiem stories may look like.<br /> If I'm about to run a D&amp;D for the first time, I have a good idea of what a typical adventure is supposed to be, and I know exactly where to start: make a dungeon, fill it with monsters, put some magic loot, end with a boss fight, done. Of course, this is useful as a starting point: as the DM grows more experienced and confident, stories will probably deviate more from the standard dungeon-crawl.<br /> At least in 1st Edition you had some suggestions on the types of conflicts you could focus on, some examples of story hooks, chronicle ideas etc. That's something I find lacking in 2E.<br /> You might say that CofD gamelines tend to have a more sandbox approach: in that case, the book should provide ST advices and tools like Apocalypse World does.<br /> <br /> Another thing that would need to change in 3d ed: less Strix.<br /> Yes, they're a cool addition. But come on.<br /> Too many Strixes.<br /> There is a staggering 19, NINETEEN different Strix NPCs, and not even a SINGLE sample Ghoul or Kindred NPC.<br /> <br /> So I guess a bit more variety and wider range of ready-made stuff for beginner STs would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree and, as you said, this kind of issue applies to CoD books in general, I'm running a human chronicle, my first time as an ST and I'm not gonna lie, I just gave up on trying to program everything and just started winging it, the books give you plenty of story hooks and suggestions but skips on how you could tie them up and leave it to the ST to decide, this might be good for an experienced ST but it really doesn't help a newbie like me. This might be one of the few things WoD did better than CoD, the sandbox approach is great but takes a lot of practice and a good deal more creativity to fully get into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T06:11:51-08:00","id":1469167,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for my first real delving into ST territory I decided to go full sandbox with just main npcs and stuff necessary for the overall theme of the Chronicle (for Demons) set in place so player will be able to run wild... If we manage to find a common day to play \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T16:41:02-08:00","id":1469434,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking about something, from my understanding diablerie is supposed to be akin to consuming a vampire soul and thats scary but why only vampires? why doesn't it work for humans too for example? or even other supernaturals? I think that a system similar to the blood resonance from v5 would be a nice addition, by &quot;diablerizing&quot; a human you would get a &quot;resonance xp&quot; that can only be spent on disciplines, this would be conceptually the vampire getting stronger by consuming the souls of other living beings (of course animals wouldn't count) at the cost of their humanity (humanity 1 breaking point), this would of course be different from draining someone without diablerizing them. Now, other supernatural would offer the same benefits of diablerizing another vampire, you would get a dot of blood potency and a dot in one of their skills that are higher than yours (of course you wouldn't get dots in your disciplines). I think this would make vampires more scary without making them too OP, since, aside from the humanity cost, you would still have to overpower another splat (this might be feasible with a changeling or even an unprepared mage but a werewolf, a demon or even a promethean? good luck with that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-02-2021, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T17:27:28-08:00","id":1469441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469434#post1469434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about something, from my understanding diablerie is supposed to be akin to consuming a vampire soul and thats scary but why only vampires? why doesn't it work for humans too for example? or even other supernaturals? I think that a system similar to the blood resonance from v5 would be a nice addition, by &quot;diablerizing&quot; a human you would get a &quot;resonance xp&quot; that can only be spent on disciplines, this would be conceptually the vampire getting stronger by consuming the souls of other living beings (of course animals wouldn't count) at the cost of their humanity (humanity 1 breaking point), this would of course be different from draining someone without diablerizing them. Now, other supernatural would offer the same benefits of diablerizing another vampire, you would get a dot of blood potency and a dot in one of their skills that are higher than yours (of course you wouldn't get dots in your disciplines). I think this would make vampires more scary without making them too OP, since, aside from the humanity cost, you would still have to overpower another splat (this might be feasible with a changeling or even an unprepared mage but a werewolf, a demon or even a promethean? good luck with that).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Requiem the explanation is that vampires are the ones with their souls strongly attached to their corpses to an unusual, that is what makes it possible to be attempted in the first place. Trying to consume souls was possible, but would require either a power based upon enhancing basic capacities-conditions of kindred nature, like the apocryphal and very frowned upon &quot;Coil of the Locust&quot; within the Ordo Dracul, or some sort of obscure bloodline power, like Requiem's Tremere bloodline apparenly did. And if memory tricks me not, neither case it was as permanent as &quot;vanilla&quot; diablerie, due to differences in nature of the souls consumed.<br /> <br /> Simply put, what passes for the soul within a vampire's undead carcass - and is consumed through diablerie - is not quite the same as a human soul anymore, and the capacity for diablerie within vampires is directly connected to whatever changes in the soul when one becomes an eternally ravening but thinking, speaking &amp; walking unspoiled corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also remember how other supernaturals are <i>specially </i>incompatible with vampirism in the first place, as demonstrated by how messy attempts to embrace Garou or Awakened can be.<br /> <br /> Wraiths-risen and the &quot;Wan Kuei&quot; (that might not be canon in V5 for all i know) might make for interesting edge cases in that they <b>are </b>thinking, speaking &amp; walking shades unusually attached to the mortal world and/or their past, through either fetters &amp; passions (wraiths), corpses (risen, though far from unspoiled in many cases) and &quot;wan kuei&quot; (that even though they fit the whole bill, by the book could <b>not</b> commit or suffer diablerie, for reasons).<br /> <br /> Aditionally, in VtM's case, there's also the extra complication - at least if one believes in the noddist/caine narrative - that &quot;consumption of the Heart's Blood&quot; was supposedly one of the angelic-divine-whatever curses bestowed upon Caine, to make all its undead &quot;descendants&quot; hunger for him and each other, suffering much conflict &amp; misery for it and if taken as fact, as direct a statement as possible of Diablerie as a cainite-only thing. but that one completely depends on &quot;all kindred descend from Cain, who was cursed by the biblical god/its angels&quot; as a true fact, so take it with a gram (or whole sack, in my case) of salt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Holy brainfarts, for some stupid reason i had it in my mind that i was answering a v5 thread instead of Requiem, leading to a number of weird in retrospect segues. Whatever, the first two paragraphs work for both. I'll leave as is in case some VtM fans interested in diablerie or soul-eating come by. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-02-2021, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T17:33:51-08:00","id":1469444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469434#post1469434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about something, from my understanding diablerie is supposed to be akin to consuming a vampire soul and thats scary but why only vampires? why doesn't it work for humans too for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are at least two pieces of developed talent on the books for exactly that. It's optional for a reason and tends to have fewer returns than committing the Amaranth on another vampire. It's more of a curiosity than anything, because if a vampire wants to make a mortal a part of themselves they usually start by feeding on them, making them a ghoul, and/or making them a vampire; you can't get more of them if you drink them down to the roots, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this would make vampires more scary without making them too OP, since, aside from the humanity cost, you would still have to overpower another splat (this might be feasible with a changeling or even an unprepared mage but a werewolf, a demon or even a promethean? good luck with that). </div> </div> </div>I will point out that the Player's Guide to the Contagion makes plainer the fact that vampires share the distinction of &quot;can straight-up yank out your soul and destroy you&quot; with Unchained demons, who can't wrestle it out of your unconscious spirit and instead need a willingly-given (albeit coercion is fair game, but mind control is not) signature (in blood) on a pact whose terms lay out when they're allowed to repossess your identity.<br /> <br /> The next-closest alternative is the Tremere, who get the ability to literally pull your soul out of your body at sufficient levels of power but don't destroy you by doing so and can put it back or supply a replacement; particularly powerful ones can do so with the souls of vampires, werewolves, and changelings in addition to mages and mortals, but the Tremere are a particularly ruthless group of mages who've altered their template in the specific pursuit of mastering The Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T18:27:38-08:00","id":1469455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469444#post1469444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are at least two pieces of developed talent on the books for exactly that. It's optional for a reason and tends to have fewer returns than committing the Amaranth on another vampire. It's more of a curiosity than anything, because if a vampire wants to make a mortal a part of themselves they usually start by feeding on them, making them a ghoul, and/or making them a vampire; you can't get more of them if you drink them down to the roots, after all.<br /> <br /> I will point out that the Player's Guide to the Contagion makes plainer the fact that vampires share the distinction of &quot;can straight-up yank out your soul and destroy you&quot; with Unchained demons, who can't wrestle it out of your unconscious spirit and instead need a willingly-given (albeit coercion is fair game, but mind control is not) signature (in blood) on a pact whose terms lay out when they're allowed to repossess your identity.<br /> <br /> The next-closest alternative is the Tremere, who get the ability to literally pull your soul out of your body at sufficient levels of power but don't destroy you by doing so and can put it back or supply a replacement; particularly powerful ones can do so with the souls of vampires, werewolves, and changelings in addition to mages and mortals, but the Tremere are a particularly ruthless group of mages who've altered their template in the specific pursuit of mastering The Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you point me in which books are the talents you were talking about? I have a lot of requiem books but I missed this, regarding the contagion guide, I didn't find any mechanics that allows vampire to eat souls, is it just a flavour thing or it is intended to work as a new mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T18:50:02-08:00","id":1469457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469455#post1469455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point me in which books are the talents you were talking about? I have a lot of requiem books but I missed this, regarding the contagion guide, I didn't find any mechanics that allows vampire to eat souls, is it just a flavour thing or it is intended to work as a new mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>From memory, I think in 1e it was the Coil of the Locust from <i>Mythologies</i>, and I'm reasonably certain a 2e equivalent exists somewhere in the booklist, but my library is in shambles and will be for some time yet.<br /> <br /> Diablerie consuming the soul is definitely not just a flavor thing; the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle includes a method to simulate diablerie with powerful Death magic to remove and re-bind one vampire's soul to another in a way that's only distinguished from regular diablerie in effects by the victim not suffering Final Death and the assisting mage suffering the consequences of destroying a soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T19:30:46-08:00","id":1469459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469457#post1469457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From memory, I think in 1e it was the Coil of the Locust from <i>Mythologies</i>, and I'm reasonably certain a 2e equivalent exists somewhere in the booklist, but my library is in shambles and will be for some time yet.<br /> <br /> Diablerie consuming the soul is definitely not just a flavor thing; the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle includes a method to simulate diablerie with powerful Death magic to remove and re-bind one vampire's soul to another in a way that's only distinguished from regular diablerie in effects by the victim not suffering Final Death and the assisting mage suffering the consequences of destroying a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way of the Locust is in <b>Ordo Dracul </b>(p. 176).There's also a way to diablerize humans in <b>Thousand Years of Night</b>, and one of the Scales of Ziva can do something akin to that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T20:46:18-08:00","id":1469464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469434#post1469434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about something, from my understanding diablerie is supposed to be akin to consuming a vampire soul and thats scary but why only vampires? why doesn't it work for humans too for example? or even other supernaturals? I think that a system similar to the blood resonance from v5 would be a nice addition, by &quot;diablerizing&quot; a human you would get a &quot;resonance xp&quot; that can only be spent on disciplines, this would be conceptually the vampire getting stronger by consuming the souls of other living beings (of course animals wouldn't count) at the cost of their humanity (humanity 1 breaking point), this would of course be different from draining someone without diablerizing them. Now, other supernatural would offer the same benefits of diablerizing another vampire, you would get a dot of blood potency and a dot in one of their skills that are higher than yours (of course you wouldn't get dots in your disciplines). I think this would make vampires more scary without making them too OP, since, aside from the humanity cost, you would still have to overpower another splat (this might be feasible with a changeling or even an unprepared mage but a werewolf, a demon or even a promethean? good luck with that).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thousand Years of Night p. 98 gives rules for Diablerising humans (requires you to be at least Blood Potency 6). I could certainly see this combining with the Unnatural Affinity Merit to allow Diablerie of other splats, though I'd probably throw in some additional benefits and drawbacks for consuming say a Mage or a Werewolf's soul. I'd also give Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle a read since per that book many splats such as Sin-Eaters and Beasts don't have souls and can't be affected by Soul related Magic, which IMO would preclude Diablerie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T03:38:09-08:00","id":1469481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469464#post1469464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thousand Years of Night p. 98 gives rules for Diablerising humans (requires you to be at least Blood Potency 6). I could certainly see this combining with the Unnatural Affinity Merit to allow Diablerie of other splats, though I'd probably throw in some additional benefits and drawbacks for consuming say a Mage or a Werewolf's soul. I'd also give Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle a read since per that book many splats such as Sin-Eaters and Beasts don't have souls and can't be affected by Soul related Magic, which IMO would preclude Diablerie</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, this is very similar to what I had in mind although one xp per integrity to spend only on blood potency is too much, I think that to make such a mechanic available to all kindreds, the xp rate should be one for every 3 dot of integrity and should only be spent on disciplines otherwise you would have young licks running around at bp5 after diablerizing a couple of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T03:38:52-08:00","id":1469482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469457#post1469457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From memory, I think in 1e it was the Coil of the Locust from <i>Mythologies</i>, and I'm reasonably certain a 2e equivalent exists somewhere in the booklist, but my library is in shambles and will be for some time yet.<br /> <br /> Diablerie consuming the soul is definitely not just a flavor thing; the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle includes a method to simulate diablerie with powerful Death magic to remove and re-bind one vampire's soul to another in a way that's only distinguished from regular diablerie in effects by the victim not suffering Final Death and the assisting mage suffering the consequences of destroying a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a mage thing though, I'm talking about a vampire mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T05:05:27-08:00","id":1469489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469481#post1469481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you, this is very similar to what I had in mind although one xp per integrity to spend only on blood potency is too much, I think that to make such a mechanic available to all kindreds, the xp rate should be one for every 3 dot of integrity and should only be spent on disciplines otherwise you would have young licks running around at bp5 after diablerizing a couple of mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it's probably too much, given that diablerizing Kindred only gives 1 exp per dot of Blood Potency. No risk of young licks making use of it though, you explicitly have to be Blood Potency 6+ to use it. I think I would probably keep it to 1 exp per dot of the power stat for other splats, and for mortals maybe 1 exp per 2 Integrity, meaning diablerising a saintly person gets you an instant Blood Potency increase","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T05:13:38-08:00","id":1469490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469489#post1469489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree it's probably too much, given that diablerizing Kindred only gives 1 exp per dot of Blood Potency. No risk of young licks making use of it though, you explicitly have to be Blood Potency 6+ to use it. I think I would probably keep it to 1 exp per dot of the power stat for other splats, and for mortals maybe 1 exp per 2 Integrity, meaning diablerising a saintly person gets you an instant Blood Potency increase</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would eliminate the blood potency 6+ requirement and making it available to all vampires, it would make all vampires more scary without breaking them too much since using such a mechanic would be a breaking point akin to a standard diablerie with addiction and everything that comes with it, not something to do lightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T09:51:49-08:00","id":1469500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469482#post1469482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a mage thing though, I'm talking about a vampire mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mage is one of the few lines that makes the distinction of what a soul is; vampires have souls sufficiently close to those of mortals that mages only need the same type of magic they would use to remove another mage's soul to meddle with them, including binding them to another vampire (when binding a soul to something does not normally destroy it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T10:02:27-08:00","id":1469502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469500#post1469500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mage is one of the few lines that makes the distinction of what a soul is; vampires have souls sufficiently close to those of mortals that mages only need the same type of magic they would use to remove another mage's soul to meddle with them, including binding them to another vampire (when binding a soul to something does not normally destroy it).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok but how has this anything to do with what I wrote? cool mages can do it (I would be more surprised to find out that they can't do something) but I'm talking about vampires diablerizing humans, there is already a mechanic like this in a thousand years of night and I think that, should a 3rd edition ever be made, converting this mechanic (with some nerfing regarding the xp you get) and making it available to all vampires would help making vampires scarier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T13:38:03-08:00","id":1469520,"title":"","content":"I don't think a core mechanic available to every vampire about devouring human souls would be a good idea. Too much tangential problems waiting to arise.<br /> <br /> First, that won't be the same as normal diablerie. Normal diablerie involves overpowering your equals, while this would involve overpowering your prey. The current downsides of diablerie simply aren't enough to hold off the sheer potential for easy abuse.<br /> <br /> Diablerizing is a risky proposition at best. Victimizing mortals is your nightly meal.<br /> <br /> Second it isn't just scarier, it is a huge change in themes for the game. It is more on the themes of Demon than Vampire. As monsters, Vampires are a take on cannibalism, and the Diablerie works on this aspect by cannibalizing your equals. Mortals you already cannibalize by eating their blood and life. What do you add to the theme with also eating souls?<br /> <br /> By the way, it won't even mean much to mortals. Vampires have, among themselves, ways to witness to the horror of diablerie. The victim is destroyed in a weird way and the criminal bears the marks of the crime for other vampires to see, a crime against their own. Mortals aren't expected to see anything that distinguishes Death by Bloodsucking from Death by Soulsucking.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't mortals, so even if they witness the effects, it just isn't the same impact, instead it may diminish the impact of diablerie by contrast.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat aside, I don't understand why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> is insisting on the Mage aspect that don't quite relate to the topic (although it is an interesting bit to contextualize it), but neither why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a> is so infuriated by this. This is pointless squabbling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T14:13:41-08:00","id":1469527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469502#post1469502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but how has this anything to do with what I wrote?</div> </div> </div> </div>You said you couldn't find anything in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle about vampires eating souls. I pointed to the part of the Guide that confirms that vampires have souls as reckoned by one of the setting's closest things to experts on souls and describes how those experts can induce a similar outcome to diablerie (i.e. the Vampire mechanic described as one vampire consuming another's soul in a way that previously could have been interpreted as simply poetic terminology) by binding a vampire's soul to a different vampire in a way that destroys it.<br /> <br /> I apologize if you were never actually asking if vampires could already eat souls, but the throughline is very straightforward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T14:16:46-08:00","id":1469528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469520#post1469520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a core mechanic available to every vampire about devouring human souls would be a good idea. Too much tangential problems waiting to arise.<br /> <br /> First, that won't be the same as normal diablerie. Normal diablerie involves overpowering your equals, while this would involve overpowering your prey. The current downsides of diablerie simply aren't enough to hold off the sheer potential for easy abuse.<br /> <br /> Diablerizing is a risky proposition at best. Victimizing mortals is your nightly meal.<br /> <br /> Second it isn't just scarier, it is a huge change in themes for the game. It is more on the themes of Demon than Vampire. As monsters, Vampires are a take on cannibalism, and the Diablerie works on this aspect by cannibalizing your equals. Mortals you already cannibalize by eating their blood and life. What do you add to the theme with also eating souls?<br /> <br /> By the way, it won't even mean much to mortals. Vampires have, among themselves, ways to witness to the horror of diablerie. The victim is destroyed in a weird way and the criminal bears the marks of the crime for other vampires to see, a crime against their own. Mortals aren't expected to see anything that distinguishes Death by Bloodsucking from Death by Soulsucking.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't mortals, so even if they witness the effects, it just isn't the same impact, instead it may diminish the impact of diablerie by contrast.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat aside, I don't understand why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> is insisting on the Mage aspect that don't quite relate to the topic (although it is an interesting bit to contextualize it), but neither why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a> is so infuriated by this. This is pointless squabbling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not infuriated by nothing and don't understand why you would think so honestly, I was just writing about a crazy idea I had about vampires being able to eat the souls of other people and splats other than their own, nothing to be angry about.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Regarding diablerie, I don't see this potential abuse regarding diablerizing mortals, it would come at a great cost and quite frankly, the reward for diablerizing mortals wouldn't be that advantageous, I mean 2 xp every 3 dots of integrity is a pretty meager reward for being slapped with a breaking point (at humanity 1 if I remember correctly and that means thay you are almost surely goin to fail your detachment roll), the tainted condition and possibly some other condition that regards diablerizing humans, it wouldn't be worth to most players to do it but it would be a possibility.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What I think diablerie would be approriate is when it comes to other splats, if you can manage to get your fangs at the throat of a powerfull monster I don't see why you shouldn't be able to diablerize them unless its a sin eater or other creature that doesn't have a soul, and even here I think that diablerie being capable of killing even such particular cases, would contribute to make vampire a lot scarier than they are now without making them op or anything.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Regarding the themes, I don't agree on that, vampire are monsters that susteing themselves by sucking life essence out of other beings, being able to diablerize humans and other splats would fit perfectly with their theme in my opinion.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T14:22:07-08:00","id":1469529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469527#post1469527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said you couldn't find anything in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle about vampires eating souls. I pointed to the part of the Guide that confirms that vampires have souls as reckoned by one of the setting's closest things to experts on souls and describes how those experts can induce a similar outcome to diablerie (i.e. the Vampire mechanic described as one vampire consuming another's soul in a way that previously could have been interpreted as simply poetic terminology) by binding a vampire's soul to a different vampire in a way that destroys it.<br /> <br /> I apologize if you were never actually asking if vampires could already eat souls, but the throughline is very straightforward.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My idea was actually about changing how diablerie works so not a ritual that mages can do to simulate its effects like the contagion guide stated, just straight up have diablerie work on humans and other splats no rituals or merits involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T15:30:03-08:00","id":1469532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469528#post1469528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I think diablerie would be approriate is when it comes to other splats, if you can manage to get your fangs at the throat of a powerfull monster I don't see why you shouldn't be able to diablerize them unless its a sin eater or other creature that doesn't have a soul, and even here I think that diablerie being capable of killing even such particular cases, would contribute to make vampire a lot scarier than they are now without making them op or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a vampire to diablerize another vampire, the vampire in question needs to be so damaged that they're torpid, and they need to make a series of rolls that all cost Willpower, and the more potent the target's blood is the more rolls it's likely to take.<br /> <br /> For a vampire to diablerize a mortal per the system in A Thousand Years of Night, the vampire needs to be an elder (i.e. they've been dead at least 150 years) and they need to have a Humanity of at least 6; the main tradeoff is that mortal diablerie addiction is not immediate and irresistible. It still works the same as normal diablerie otherwise, in that it requires drinking the victim to and beyond death.<br /> <br /> Of the splats that have souls, vampires and mortals are already covered by existing systems, werewolves can freely assume a form that regenerates faster than any feeding could drain them and quickly goes berserk thereafter, changelings can escape a grapple without rolling by spending one point of Glamour but can be rendered comatose through sufficiently advanced gaslighting, mummies' souls are spoken for by their godlike masters, and deviants' souls are so unstable that attempting to steal them has been likened to sticking your hand in a blender.<br /> <br /> The remaining splats are Prometheans (who have a burning furnace of fateful energy that may become a soul), demons (who were never actually human and who only &quot;have a soul&quot; in the sense that calling in a soul pact attaches one to them), Sin-Eaters/Bound (whose near-immortality is furnished by a powerful ghost that can manifest whenever their Health is low enough unless they successfully stop it), and beasts (whose individual soul has been overrun by the Lair of the Astral Horror that gives them their power).<br /> <br /> Diablerie doesn't kill things, it is an act that builds upon a killing. We've got established ghost-drinking bloodlines on the books, and the process by which a werewolf's Sacred Hunt can perma-kill a spirit has its analogs to the Amaranth, but the fearsome nature of consuming a soul speaks more to the fact that you were able to have somebody so at-your-mercy than to the fact their personality is now a voice in your head.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm more interested in, to be honest, is extending the process of ghouling, the geographical effects of the Predatory Aura, the vampiric use of Wyrm's Nests, the implications of Discipline powers like Oubliette and Lord of the Land, and so on as a way for powerful vampires to feed off of the land itself or otherwise facilitate weird vampire hermits living far from obvious access to people but still sustaining themselves on ambient power, esoteric prey, and the occasional windfall of unrefined blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T15:51:42-08:00","id":1469536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1469532#post1469532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a vampire to diablerize another vampire, the vampire in question needs to be so damaged that they're torpid, and they need to make a series of rolls that all cost Willpower, and the more potent the target's blood is the more rolls it's likely to take.<br /> <br /> For a vampire to diablerize a mortal per the system in A Thousand Years of Night, the vampire needs to be an elder (i.e. they've been dead at least 150 years) and they need to have a Humanity of at least 6; the main tradeoff is that mortal diablerie addiction is not immediate and irresistible. It still works the same as normal diablerie otherwise, in that it requires drinking the victim to and beyond death.<br /> <br /> Of the splats that have souls, vampires and mortals are already covered by existing systems, werewolves can freely assume a form that regenerates faster than any feeding could drain them and quickly goes berserk thereafter, changelings can escape a grapple without rolling by spending one point of Glamour but can be rendered comatose through sufficiently advanced gaslighting, mummies' souls are spoken for by their godlike masters, and deviants' souls are so unstable that attempting to steal them has been likened to sticking your hand in a blender.<br /> <br /> The remaining splats are Prometheans (who have a burning furnace of fateful energy that may become a soul), demons (who were never actually human and who only &quot;have a soul&quot; in the sense that calling in a soul pact attaches one to them), Sin-Eaters/Bound (whose near-immortality is furnished by a powerful ghost that can manifest whenever their Health is low enough unless they successfully stop it), and beasts (whose individual soul has been overrun by the Lair of the Astral Horror that gives them their power).<br /> <br /> Diablerie doesn't kill things, it is an act that builds upon a killing. We've got established ghost-drinking bloodlines on the books, and the process by which a werewolf's Sacred Hunt can perma-kill a spirit has its analogs to the Amaranth, but the fearsome nature of consuming a soul speaks more to the fact that you were able to have somebody so at-your-mercy than to the fact their personality is now a voice in your head.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm more interested in, to be honest, is extending the process of ghouling, the geographical effects of the Predatory Aura, the vampiric use of Wyrm's Nests, the implications of Discipline powers like Oubliette and Lord of the Land, and so on as a way for powerful vampires to feed off of the land itself or otherwise facilitate weird vampire hermits living far from obvious access to people but still sustaining themselves on ambient power, esoteric prey, and the occasional windfall of unrefined blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I said that it would make vampires scarier not thougher, you would still have to overpower the other splats and how you do it, its another matter entirely (you would still have to put them in such a position that they could be diablerized, either by fighting or through some other means for the truly op splats like mummies and demons) and like I wrote before, having vampires being capable of completely killing someone body and soul would add to their theme of being parasitic monsters.<br /> <br /> Regarding the ghouls and the other things you wrote, those are perfectly valid points but it seems that everybody would just settle for &quot;more of the same&quot; from an eventual 3rd edition while I would like something a little more radical, not enough to break the splat entirely but still new and fresh, vampires might be static creatures but I as a player surely am not and I particularly enjoy changes that are done right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T13:45:22-08:00","id":1470072,"title":"","content":"I just want to see a version of Requiem that is properly cleaned up. No more rules that are too vague, or scattered across several location throughout the book, or completely unbalanced, etc. Requiem seems to be really bad for this kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, I really want to see a complete overhaul of how bloodlines work. No more &quot;they're just the same as the core clan but with a fourth clan discipline&quot; or &quot;they're just the same as the core clan but has a slightly different shared philosophy&quot; or garbage like that. I want to see each bloodline be truly unique and different in some way, not just a set of character concepts you can already make with core clans. Also, give bloodlines the same treatment as Kiths got when Changeling went from 1e to 2e. In other words, make it so any clan can take any bloodline. This will remove a considerable amount of repitition and redundancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 12-09-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T12:29:30-08:00","id":1470159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470072#post1470072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to see a version of Requiem that is properly cleaned up. No more rules that are too vague, or scattered across several location throughout the book, or completely unbalanced, etc. Requiem seems to be really bad for this kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, I really want to see a complete overhaul of how bloodlines work. No more &quot;they're just the same as the core clan but with a fourth clan discipline&quot; or &quot;they're just the same as the core clan but has a slightly different shared philosophy&quot; or garbage like that. I want to see each bloodline be truly unique and different in some way, not just a set of character concepts you can already make with core clans. Also, give bloodlines the same treatment as Kiths got when Changeling went from 1e to 2e. In other words, make it so any clan can take any bloodline. This will remove a considerable amount of repitition and redundancy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you think that Requiem is a mess, you should check the Werewolf and Mage books, this kind of vagueness is common to all the splats really.<br /> <br /> Regarding bloodlines, I think that an approach similar to Deviants might be a better course of action, instead of being the basic clans with an extra discipline and a few more limitations like they are now, they might actually be &quot;adaptations&quot; that each individual vampire can develop on his own (with a relative penalty). You would have to scrap all of the bloodlines fluff but since it seems that most people are not happy with them, that might not be such a great loss anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T00:04:26-08:00","id":1470194,"title":"","content":"Are bloodlines really that disliked ? As far as I could tell, I really liked them. And removing the clan lineage through them would basically mean all Bloodlines would be erased and you'd have to create something distinct. Because if nott largely Clan restricted (I never liked the lines open to all Clans) then you just create a sort of sub-Covenant anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 12-11-2021, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T00:27:59-08:00","id":1470195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470194#post1470194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are bloodlines really that disliked ? As far as I could tell, I really liked them. And removing the clan lineage through them would basically mean all Bloodlines would be erased and you'd have to create something distinct. Because if nott largely Clan restricted (I never liked the lines open to all Clans) then you just create a sort of sub-Covenant anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like Bloodlines conceptually. I'm not a huge fan of any of the ones that have been published for 2nd edition, but the updated 1e Bloodlines on Storyteller's Vault from NMD are fantastic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T02:53:32-08:00","id":1470200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470194#post1470194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are bloodlines really that disliked ? As far as I could tell, I really liked them. And removing the clan lineage through them would basically mean all Bloodlines would be erased and you'd have to create something distinct. Because if nott largely Clan restricted (I never liked the lines open to all Clans) then you just create a sort of sub-Covenant anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don''t dislike many individual Bloodlines, but I do think the Bloodline concept is inherently bad/limiting for the game. Bloodlines are used to represent everything from lineages, sub-Covenant factions, curses, and other weird quirks of the Blood, but since they're all sharing a singular slot on the character sheet they're all mutually exclusive. It simply doesn't make sense that a Daeva from a prestigious lineage of nobles can't make a deal with a demon who specifically looks for those with high ambition, or that an Ordo scholar who researches how to eat ghosts is immune to the madness cursing their Clan despite their insane field of research. Oh, and only Ventrue are able to research ghost-eating for some reason.<br /> (Only made slightly better that the curse of madness was changed to not being a bloodline later in 1e.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T02:57:58-08:00","id":1470201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470200#post1470200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don''t dislike many individual Bloodlines, but I do think the Bloodline concept is inherently bad for the game. Bloodlines are used to represent everything from lineages, sub-Covenant factions, curses, and other weird quirks of the Blood, but since they're all sharing a singular slot on the character sheet they're all mutually exclusive. It simply doesn't make sense that a Daeva from a prestigious lineage of nobles can't make a deal with a demon who specifically looks for those with high ambition, or that an Ordo scholar who researches how to eat ghosts is immune to the madness cursing their Clan despite their insane field of research. Oh, and only Ventrue are able to research ghost-eating for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never gave much thought to the issue before, but there's also the matter of some degree of mix-up/redundancy between bloodline powers &amp; weaknesses with certain merit trees and built-in colaterals, to boot. Kindred Medium &amp; Ghost-eating as merits x the Dragolescu Essentiaphagia discipline in particular comes to mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T03:15:52-08:00","id":1470205,"title":"","content":"I don't think bloodlines should be removed, and I definitely don't think they should be unbound from blood, but I do think they should be narrowed down and focused into actual bloodlines that maintain the themes of ancestry and blood and lineage over the eons one would expect from Vampires rather than obscure quirks and weird variants.<br /> <br /> There is a game called Artesia that has a lineage ruleset where you get stats and bonuses from your ancestry and can also, when suitably powerful, add to that lineage/bonus for your own offspring.<br /> <br /> Something like that would be nice, where you get bonuses from your Sire (players could maybe choose a bonus for this much like some splats choose a bonus for their Clan-equivalent) and can, upon reaching a certain BP, enhance or modify their lineage for their own Childer. I don't really think they need all these special mechanics unique to each bloodline like the Kerberoi, neat as these special mechanics may be.<br /> <br /> It should enhance the themes of the game rather than be a prestige class just because all splats need prestige classes for some reason (Legacy, Entitlements, etc, etc, etc.) I feel like a bloodline should make you feel a part of what came before you and like you are contributing to what comes after. Current bloodlines just feel like layering another set of powers which are cool but don't seem to really have a place or reason for existing other than being cool.<br /> <br /> I don't really think Vampire needs this kind of prestige class. A sufficiently old Vampire is suitably unique and terrifying just from the Devotions and allies and resources and powers they create and gather over time and knowledge they've accrued without needing some additional template layered on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T03:32:12-08:00","id":1470206,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Bloodline stuff is like those \u201cYou can have only one of a curse\u201d thing. You mutate the Curse of the Blood on you in one way, <i>any</i> way, then you lock yourself out of further curses on the same \u2018slot\u2019.<br /> <br /> Hey, werewolves are described as having several separate spiritual \u2018slots\u2019 for pack totems, Lodge totems, Tribal patronage, and Luna to fit it. Maybe vampires have a similar ladder of curses on them based on Clan, Bloodline, and personalized inHumanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T03:45:10-08:00","id":1470207,"title":"","content":"I also think that's a good idea, but I also don't want to lose out on the other 80% of Bloodlines we have today. I think Bloodlines should be split into multiple different systems, kinda like how changelings are changed and individualised through everything between Kiths, Mantles, Entitlements and regular Merits.<br /> You can have lineages that comes with certain advantages and disadvantages represented through either Merits or a minor standardised system.<br /> You can have sub-factions in Covenants be represented through Merits, like those that already exist for specific positions or as MCI-style Merits.<br /> You can have Curses of the Blood be represented through Persistent Conditions, or through other means. They're kinda supposed to be unique and terrifying so no standardised systems would/could work.<br /> You can have unique Disciplines unlinked from specific Bloodlines/Clans, similar to Blood Tenebrous or Breath-Drinking, but with inherent drawbacks that comes from learning them. If they're associated with specific groups, then they could be highly guarded secrets and/or have the groups receive an XP discount through their associated Merits.<br /> You can have other unique concepts be their own things and not force them into a specific system.<br /> <br /> And now you could play a vampire of a prestigious lineage who has joined a small faction whose ideologies resonate with her while she tries to hide the curse in her blood from others. Or any other kind of combination you'd want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T16:48:18-08:00","id":1470248,"title":"","content":"Personally I never bothered with bloodlines, I think that they are not worth the considerable flaws they come with, vampires already have to deal with sunlight, their clan curse and whatever bane they might get during their requiem, why add to all of this for an extra discipline that might not even be unique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T02:54:30-08:00","id":1470593,"title":"","content":"What i want to see the vampire, is reflected how i saw people playing vampire, this is how i saw people playing vampire for many years:<br /> - ditch the personal drama and humanity (make the stat without mechanic wheight), rarely people use it<br /> <br /> - embrace what vampire is: a mafia game of immortal criminals fighting eachother<br /> - embrace: the antagonist for vampires are other vampires<br /> - a system of favors/debt mixed with status, reflecting the corruption of vampire society<br /> - focus on the convenants, you dont even need clans, just do blodlines<br /> - ditch the hole predator's mark and blood potency sleep<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","name":"avoloch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:35:37-08:00","id":1470600,"title":"","content":"SORRY ABOUT MY ENGLISH <br /> i also think that blood potency dont help the game, the need for torpor could came from the deep sleep heals the mind<br /> from centuries of boredom and trauma, give novelty and refresh the brain instead of dealing with blood potency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","name":"avoloch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:54:51-08:00","id":1470603,"title":"","content":"That seems... like an odd suggestion. Lowering Blood Potency is only one reason to enter torpor, and Blood Potency never requires you to enter torpor; it's a choice vampires make to sacrifice power and time to enable them to have an easier time with Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:04:14-08:00","id":1470605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470603#post1470603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems... like an odd suggestion. Lowering Blood Potency is only one reason to enter torpor, and Blood Potency never requires you to enter torpor; it's a choice vampires make to sacrifice power and time to enable them to have an easier time with Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES, and people that i game with don\u00b4t like it, because you need to sacrifice power<br /> 90% of people are powergamers<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","name":"avoloch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:30:03-08:00","id":1470610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avoloch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470605#post1470605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YES, and people that i game with don\u00b4t like it, because you need to sacrifice power<br /> 90% of people are powergamers</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of ways to deal with high BP. <br /> High BP doesn't mean only physical and raw power but also, if character is well played, servants (also kindred), cults etc.<br /> <br /> Your high covenant's status characters may have monthly rituals where other kindred spill blood as a tribute on the soil where he sank (Protean 1). May store kindred vitae in Simulacrum (Theban sorcery 1). They may build up more deviant situation where they have reavenant kept as blood bags. <br /> There are charthian or Invictus means to deal with feeding on kindred's vitae without blood bond.<br /> <br /> High BP vampires may prey on low status kindred as Monsters among Monsters.<br /> <br /> You may set up perversion - both kindred bound each other with a vinculum.<br /> <br /> If characters want easy life they should be ready to sacrifice a bit of physical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:15:32-08:00","id":1470617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avoloch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470593#post1470593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i want to see the vampire, is reflected how i saw people playing vampire, this is how i saw people playing vampire for many years:</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with most of those suggestions is that they ditch options and play styles instead of creating them. You may not have seen much people that play with those concepts, I did. But a side box talking about taking off pieces of the system that don't fit your style, that is pretty much valid.<br /> <br /> One thing I must agree, a lot of things in the game are there because they're VtM's heritage, including a lot of themes, but by now they're already adapted to a VtR feel. Humanity and Blood Potency are linked to VtM-born themes, even when they're inverted (as in torpor here reducing BP).<br /> <br /> But seriously, aside from the system of favors and debt, it seems more like you want to use this rule system to play with vampires, but don't actually like this specific vampire game. Which isn't a problem in the least, just a fact, but not something that many people will agree with you here. At least not in the sense of ditching 2/3 of the game to make it just an immortal mob power fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T10:08:52-08:00","id":1470637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avoloch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470593#post1470593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i want to see the vampire, is reflected how i saw people playing vampire, this is how i saw people playing vampire for many years:<br /> - ditch the personal drama and humanity (make the stat without mechanic wheight), rarely people use it<br /> <br /> - embrace what vampire is: a mafia game of immortal criminals fighting eachother<br /> - embrace: the antagonist for vampires are other vampires<br /> - a system of favors/debt mixed with status, reflecting the corruption of vampire society<br /> - focus on the convenants, you dont even need clans, just do blodlines<br /> - ditch the hole predator's mark and blood potency sleep<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have some pretty radical ideas about what should be changed about Requiem but what you are describing would lead to an entirely different game IMO.<br /> <br /> I have been in quite a few Requiem games and I would say that the &quot;mafia style&quot; games were the most boring and were run by people who were more familiar with Masquerade than Requiem, not saying that you couldn't run something similar but frankly, you would basically waste 2/3 of the setting by reducing it to a mere mafia game.<br /> <br /> The favors/debt thing is already kinda in it and can be played in story quite easily but if you meant of making it an official mechanic than I'm all up for it, it never hurts to have detailed rules about systems and mechanics instead of the vagueness that seem to be standard operating procedure for all of the CoD lines.<br /> <br /> Regarding the focus on the covenants, you already can do this, the way the game is written, nothing stops you from having your city focused on covenants politics without clans interference, no need to remove clans in favour of bloodlines (especially because the latters are not what I would call the most &quot;loved&quot; part of the game).<br /> <br /> I don't quite understand what you mean with predator's mark, are you talking about predatory aura? whats wrong with that?<br /> <br /> Regarding blood potency I don't see where the problem is, staying into torpor long enough to drop a blood potency level (50 years if I remember correctly) has to be something that the players want, if you are beaten into torpor, unless you have very low humanity, you are going to be able to wake up way before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T10:21:20-08:00","id":1470638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470637#post1470637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the focus on the covenants, you already can do this, the way the game is written, nothing stops you from having your city focused on covenants politics without clans interference, no need to remove clans in favour of bloodlines (especially because the latters are not what I would call the most &quot;loved&quot; part of the game).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm concerned, Clan politics is basically absent by default. There's the Clan Status Merit, but very little fluff and no other mechanics to back up any sort of Clan organisations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470637#post1470637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding blood potency I don't see where the problem is, staying into torpor long enough to drop a blood potency level (50 years if I remember correctly) has to be something that the players want, if you are beaten into torpor, unless you have very low humanity, you are going to be able to wake up way before.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 25 years.<br /> For PCs it's a complete non-issue*, but it means that whenever you want an ancient elder to wake up and disturb the peace or just have the players find the resting place of such an elder, they'll always wake up with BP1.<br /> <br /> *An exception is historical games where time skips are used to fastforward through large time spans. We're planning such a game right now and we'll have to completely rework everything relating to BP changes so that we have a good progression from year ~410 to current day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T10:50:05-08:00","id":1470642,"title":"","content":"I somehow consider it more likely that when CofD 3e rolls around, Paradox will sell it to Onyx Path and it will switch to Storypath to keep things siloed.<br /> <br /> I really don't get why Paradox seems fine letting CofD slow down to a crawl. They're not relying on Onyx Path for the WoD 5e stuff, CofD development is clearly something that benefits WoD 5e developments, and a successful CofD makes Paradox money for basically doing nothing. I get not just rubbing stamping things but... eh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T11:05:50-08:00","id":1470644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470638#post1470638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I'm concerned, Clan politics is basically absent by default. There's the Clan Status Merit, but very little fluff and no other mechanics to back up any sort of Clan organisations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's 25 years.<br /> For PCs it's a complete non-issue*, but it means that whenever you want an ancient elder to wake up and disturb the peace or just have the players find the resting place of such an elder, they'll always wake up with BP1.<br /> <br /> *An exception is historical games where time skips are used to fastforward through large time spans. We're planning such a game right now and we'll have to completely rework everything relating to BP changes so that we have a good progression from year ~410 to current day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Clan politics popped up in a couple of games I was in although the majority mostly paid lip service to it and focused on the covenants, the exceptions were in cities that had a predominance of a certain clan in a covenant (one game in particular had the vast majority of the Crones being daevas).<br /> <br /> I was in a game that started in the 1500's and gradually progressed to the modern day (lasted about two years in real life), after the first months when the ST decided to have the first time skip, we had another session zero where we discussed what we would have wanted from the game and how we should approach the whole BP thing, we decided to transition to the elder template (a thousand years of night was the basis for everything elder related) and basically do what was more in character. My character was a nosferatu and he went into voluntary torpor to keep his BP at 5 and so did our Daeva, our ventrue had the highest at 7 but had to get into the graces of the ordu to get the scales for allowing him to subsist on human blood because it was getting harder to feed, our gangrel went on a crusade against a large werewolf pack when he was at BP 6 but ended up in torpor following a last stand against a ridiculously badass Rahu and decided to drop at BP 4 for his &quot;repentant monster&quot; phase.<br /> The game was very character focused without the PC focusing too much on their power level and preferring to pursue their in character objective, it was far less unbalanced than you would immagine (although don't expect for humans or even most other supernaturals to be a real threat to you, both physically and powerwise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T02:41:44-08:00","id":1470991,"title":"","content":"how do you guys think people really play vampire requiem?<br /> for me people play in one of this styles:<br /> - mafia / political intrigue<br /> - vampire: the x man<br /> - my litle drama class ( for one session and then gets bored)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","name":"avoloch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T03:49:54-08:00","id":1470996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avoloch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470991#post1470991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do you guys think people really play vampire requiem?<br /> for me people play in one of this styles:<br /> - mafia / political intrigue<br /> - vampire: the x man<br /> - my litle drama class ( for one session and then gets bored)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can speak to this, since I'm running a Requiem game right now. It's not really any of these styles. In our game, the Coterie have recently graduated from being Ancilla to being the leaders of their city (Bath circa 500 AD, using the Arthur's Brittannia Dark Era) and of their respective Covenants. The player characters aren't directly at cross purposes with each other, and there are a lot of outside factors that are causing them to need to work together, including an army coming to besiege their city.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless there's an entertaining amount of backstabbing going on. In our game, I would say about 50% of scenes have two or more characters together in the same scene, and about 50% are just one character interacting with NPCs. This means characters have a lot of opportunities to lie or misdirect. Even better, sometimes two or more characters are in on the same lie, and honestly I'm pretty impressed that the players are able to keep their character knowledge straight and remember who knows what.<br /> <br /> So while a lot of the time the players are working broadly in concert with each other, there are also lots of political shenanigans happening behind the scenes. For example, the former Prince of the city recently &quot;went missing&quot;. The players took the opportunity to seize power by forming a council. Now, the player who is leader of the Circle of the Crone knows what happened to the Prince and knows that she's not coming back. But he also didn't want the Lancea et Sanctum to get a spot on the Council. So he argued that while they could fill the empty Council positions (such as Sheriff, Augur, and Keeper of Elysium) they couldn't create any new ones since only the Prince could do that and the Prince is currently missing. The compromise they came to is that the Lance could send a representative (the Lancea et Sanctum player character) but they are only an observer and can't actually vote on anything.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to wrapping up this story and doing a time skip into the future, since I think that will lead to a lot more opportunities for the players to directly antagonize one another. But I still don't see it ever becoming a full political intrigue game since there's always some external force or threat that the Coterie have to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T03:58:42-08:00","id":1470998,"title":"","content":"I think that's a solid example of a political game. The fact that external factors triggers all the intriguing is less relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T11:16:28-08:00","id":1471019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avoloch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470991#post1470991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do you guys think people really play vampire requiem?<br /> for me people play in one of this styles:<br /> - mafia / political intrigue<br /> - vampire: the x man<br /> - my litle drama class ( for one session and then gets bored)</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that those are such broad, ill defined strokes that you can shove almost any story whatsoever into one of those, so I don't see the point beyond giving derogatory nicknames to play styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T03:36:37-08:00","id":1471076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1470996#post1470996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can speak to this, since I'm running a Requiem game right now. It's not really any of these styles. In our game, the Coterie have recently graduated from being Ancilla to being the leaders of their city (Bath circa 500 AD, using the Arthur's Brittannia Dark Era) and of their respective Covenants. The player characters aren't directly at cross purposes with each other, and there are a lot of outside factors that are causing them to need to work together, including an army coming to besiege their city.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless there's an entertaining amount of backstabbing going on. In our game, I would say about 50% of scenes have two or more characters together in the same scene, and about 50% are just one character interacting with NPCs. This means characters have a lot of opportunities to lie or misdirect. Even better, sometimes two or more characters are in on the same lie, and honestly I'm pretty impressed that the players are able to keep their character knowledge straight and remember who knows what.<br /> <br /> So while a lot of the time the players are working broadly in concert with each other, there are also lots of political shenanigans happening behind the scenes. For example, the former Prince of the city recently &quot;went missing&quot;. The players took the opportunity to seize power by forming a council. Now, the player who is leader of the Circle of the Crone knows what happened to the Prince and knows that she's not coming back. But he also didn't want the Lancea et Sanctum to get a spot on the Council. So he argued that while they could fill the empty Council positions (such as Sheriff, Augur, and Keeper of Elysium) they couldn't create any new ones since only the Prince could do that and the Prince is currently missing. The compromise they came to is that the Lance could send a representative (the Lancea et Sanctum player character) but they are only an observer and can't actually vote on anything.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to wrapping up this story and doing a time skip into the future, since I think that will lead to a lot more opportunities for the players to directly antagonize one another. But I still don't see it ever becoming a full political intrigue game since there's always some external force or threat that the Coterie have to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>VERY FUN, VERY POLITICAL<br /> my last game was about a group of carthians who gave a coup on an invictus prince and instaled a democracy<br /> the players where embraced to make sure people voted ''the right way''<br /> in their mission they learned about the vampires of the city and what everyone wanted<br /> i missed some, status / debt system that can reflec how corrupt vampires are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","name":"avoloch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T12:22:16-08:00","id":1471789,"title":"","content":"If there was ever a Requiem 3rd edition, this is the setting update I'd like to see. <br /> <br /> The masquerade falls and vampires become known to the population. It would be similiar to the True Blood TV show idea. You could still have political intigue and I think it's more inline with the zeitgest of today. It would also set itself apart from Vampire the Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T13:15:50-08:00","id":1471791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drumheller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1471789#post1471789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was ever a Requiem 3rd edition, this is the setting update I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> The masquerade falls and vampires become known to the population. It would be similiar to the True Blood TV show idea. You could still have political intigue and I think it's more inline with the zeitgest of today. It would also set itself apart from Vampire the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't put into words how I despise True Blood but the idea is certainly interesting, in the CoD setting its more or less implied that people are aware that something is wrong so actually stop pretending and making the world at large aware that supernaturals exists (not just vampires, I am really curious how changelings would be perceived by the public) would certainly be an interesting developement and help differentiate CoD from WoD although I have no idea how this would be accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T13:32:14-08:00","id":1471793,"title":"","content":"That's not really an &quot;update&quot; as much as a &quot;radical change to the assumptions of the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides, we've already gotten &quot;what if the Masquerade ended?&quot; in late 1e supplements for people that want to do that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T13:37:56-08:00","id":1471794,"title":"","content":"Certainly True Blood is an acquired taste. I believe their was discussion of a future suppliment covering this idea, or it was a shard setting in one of the books.<br /> <br /> To me, the concept of the masquerade seems a product of a different time. In our world today, the problems and notorious public figures are in plain sight. A new Requiem setting with vampires in plain sight. I could see the Invictus undertaking a program to gaslight the human population, &quot;We are your friends and being a vampire is the natural order of things and your link to the past&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":85,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","user":"Drumheller","date":". 01-04-2022, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T13:47:21-08:00","id":1471796,"title":"","content":"To be honest I always found the idea of a masquerade in modern times ridiculous since there is no way that something like the existence of supernaturals could remain hidden, on the other hand I have trouble imagining how something like this could be pulled off story wise, maybe by having a &quot;soft&quot; masquerade breach akin to what happen in V5 where only the world governments would have knowledge of the supernatural at large although, if task force valkyrie is of any indication, they kinda do already but it would be interesting to expand on this aspect for sure, on the other hand this would make the game too similar to V5, something that I'm personally against for a variety of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T17:00:57-08:00","id":1471811,"title":"","content":"It feels like VtM assumptions about how the Masquerade works is coming into this. VtR's idea is not some giant vampire conspiracy, though vampires work towards this end, that creates the Masquerade: humans do. Humans in the CofD all, on some instinctive level, know the supernatural exists, but telling the supernatural that gets you killed (or worse). It is a &quot;soft&quot; Masquerade enforced by dozens of thousands of years of evolutionary pressure favoring humans that are in a perpetual state of subconscious denial about the world they truly live in.<br /> <br /> Also things like The Lie in Mage that can further explain how humans have become more and more blind to the truth over time.<br /> <br /> As has been noted, repeatedly, when discussing this for the CofD, there's a reason why the 2e core book's character creation section tells people playing normal humans to still come up with supernatural events their character has brushed up against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T17:44:57-08:00","id":1471813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drumheller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1471789#post1471789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was ever a Requiem 3rd edition, this is the setting update I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> The masquerade falls and vampires become known to the population. It would be similiar to the True Blood TV show idea. You could still have political intigue and I think it's more inline with the zeitgest of today. It would also set itself apart from Vampire the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, they already know.<br /> <br /> Most people, deep down, know vampires are real. You can't live in the Chronicles of Darkness without having a sense that something is deeply <i>wrong </i>with the world, and that supernatural beings are part of it. No, you don't say it out loud, because A) there's a literal machine god that maintains a vicious false status quo and B) your life will be a lot better if you don't piss off the vampires who might be listening in. Why go asking for trouble? And like, they're rare, right? Probably all died out a long time ago, or they only come out on a full moon...or maybe they all just live with the homeless people, snacking on derelicts. They certainly won't come for you, with your dead bolt and your security system. Why worry about it. Why even talk about it.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is about <i>who </i>is a vampire. Steve down the hall? Definitely not a vampire. You had coffee with him that one time! And vampires don't eat, so he can't be one. Vampires don't watch football with you on Sunday (they have to sleep on Sunday, right?) They don't bring sick guac to game night (garlic! Garlic is in guac!) No. Steve is NOT a vampire.*<br /> <br /> Does <i>everyone </i>know vampires are real? Well, most people know sharks are real, but we don't spend a lot of time thinking about them. However, you also know not to go swimming alone with a bloody wound, just like you <i>never </i>patronize that night club on 7th Street.<br /> <br /> But shark attacks still happen, no matter who tells us to never swim alone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Steve is the prince.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-05-2022, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T03:31:16-08:00","id":1471837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1471813#post1471813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, they already know.<br /> <br /> Most people, deep down, know vampires are real. You can't live in the Chronicles of Darkness without having a sense that something is deeply <i>wrong </i>with the world, and that supernatural beings are part of it. No, you don't say it out loud, because A) there's a literal machine god that maintains a vicious false status quo and B) your life will be a lot better if you don't piss off the vampires who might be listening in. Why go asking for trouble? And like, they're rare, right? Probably all died out a long time ago, or they only come out on a full moon...or maybe they all just live with the homeless people, snacking on derelicts. They certainly won't come for you, with your dead bolt and your security system. Why worry about it. Why even talk about it.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is about <i>who </i>is a vampire. Steve down the hall? Definitely not a vampire. You had coffee with him that one time! And vampires don't eat, so he can't be one. Vampires don't watch football with you on Sunday (they have to sleep on Sunday, right?) They don't bring sick guac to game night (garlic! Garlic is in guac!) No. Steve is NOT a vampire.*<br /> <br /> Does <i>everyone </i>know vampires are real? Well, most people know sharks are real, but we don't spend a lot of time thinking about them. However, you also know not to go swimming alone with a bloody wound, just like you <i>never </i>patronize that night club on 7th Street.<br /> <br /> But shark attacks still happen, no matter who tells us to never swim alone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Steve is the prince.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Steve being the prince is a nice touch, now that I think of it, I wouldn't mind a little paragraph in an eventual 3rd edition describing what vamps do in their &quot;free time&quot;, just for roleplaying purposes if anything else.<br /> <br /> I would guess that not all vampires engages in the danse, hell anyone with a little sense would try to steer clear of it, most neonates likely won't have the choice since they need the support of the covenants to survive but I could see an ancilla or an elder saying &quot;fuck it&quot; and just do his own thing, a 1000 years of night had something like this when describing how a newly awakened elder would get reacquainted with the world after a long torpor but I guess what I'm looking for is a few more info into how the unaligned spend their nights and maybe some story hooks to run a chronicle this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T13:42:29-08:00","id":1471856,"title":"","content":"Steve is keeping up with his Touchstone... even Princes need to do that (even if maybe, as a Prince, Steve has moved on from one specific human to the local sports team and thus spends time watching football with other fans).<br /> <br /> While it could use more explicit discussion, sure, the fact that vampires don't naturally recover Willpower by resting means their free time is going to mostly involve replacing rest and relaxation activities will Willpower recovering ones... which can also easily be breaks from vampire politics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T15:01:25-08:00","id":1471863,"title":"","content":"Touchstones are another thing I would like to be expanded upon, a more detailed system of interactions that would give bonuses depending on how the interaction goes, spending a lovely night with your mortal fiance, watching the game with your college roommate or even just taking your father's old car for a ride would all remind you of your humanity and result in a variety of positive conditions to help mitigate frenzy or detachment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T15:47:45-08:00","id":1471871,"title":"","content":"Eh... the game needs less Conditions, not more. Complexity needs to serve a purpose for the fun of playing the game, not just add a lot of bookwork to get to basically the same results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T16:11:27-08:00","id":1471874,"title":"","content":"I disagree, Conditions are a very interesting part of CoD that can help representing the impact that the world has on the characters, I personally never felt they were out of place, I wouldn't have a problem with more conditions if done properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T16:28:10-08:00","id":1471875,"title":"","content":"I would rather remove Conditions entirely. They were meant to lower bookkeeping, but they just add to it. They are difficult to track and easy to forget entirely when one runs online. I'm sure it's better for face-to-face games, but I'm somewhat curious if that is even the majority anymore these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T16:51:03-08:00","id":1471878,"title":"","content":"I feel like I'm going to repeat myself here...<br /> <br /> There should only be ~5 mundane Condition templates, with a clear guide on how each can be used for positive, mixed, or negative Conditions, how they look as normal or persistent, and what to use each template for.<br /> <br /> One of the problem with tracking them, is that there's dozens of them, and they all work on custom rules. If your Conditions are listed: [Name] ([impact][permutation]} they're much easier to remember and use. &quot;Swooning: Bob (mixed resistance)&quot; as long as &quot;mixed&quot; and &quot;resistance&quot; are well defined with simple mechanics is a lot easier than just having Swooning and trying to remember what that means.<br /> <br /> Even without me defining those terms, it's already easy to assume that &quot;mixed resistance&quot; with a word like Swooning means you get a bonus or a penalty to your Resistance Attributes depending on how the action triggering resistance plays off of Bob.<br /> <br /> Then you have a lot more room for a few supernatural specific Conditions, which are also now much easier to find, for Auras, Disciplines, and so on to impart. And that's even if they really need special mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T17:05:06-08:00","id":1471882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1471875#post1471875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather remove Conditions entirely. They were meant to lower bookkeeping, but they just add to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to play face to face and I pretty much felt like this.<br /> <br /> The core idea of Conditions is neat. I think the basic model of &quot;do X and discard this for beat&quot; is a fine example of how they should really work. They should have as little hard rules on them as possible and just be flexible instead.<br /> <br /> Powers that just look for the Name of the Condition, like the Manifestations do, also help as you only have to worry about the power rules instead of the rules from the Condition you're tracking.<br /> <br /> But putting specific rules on every one of them? That creates a lot of bookkeeping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:00:06-08:00","id":1474273,"title":"","content":"i think D&amp;D approach the conditions perfectly, is the basic things that can affect a person like:<br /> poisoned<br /> proned<br /> grabbed<br /> frightened<br /> <br /> the basic conditions should be solid to be usefull for the DM<br /> i thin you need some real solid basic conditions like 5-6 that can be used in any game<br /> like ''uncontious'' and separated very few scenario specific conditions<br /> <br /> you dont need the condition ''humbled'' for example, is too much noise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","user":"avoloch","date":". 02-09-2022, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27212-avoloch","name":"avoloch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:34:47-08:00","id":1474276,"title":"","content":"Even as someone that wants to see the base Conditions cut drastically... you're talking about Tilts. It's easy to do a short consistent list when you're only really focused on combat mechanics.<br /> <br /> CofD Conditions have to address a lot more than the physical complications that action scenes might impart.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T10:19:46-08:00","id":1474297,"title":"","content":"The point with Conditions <i>as CoD defines them</i> is to inform long term character behavior. It is less about the bonuses and penalties that come along and more about how the Condition affects how the character navigates the story.<br /> <br /> It is not that D&amp;D Conditions aren't good, it's just that as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, CoD calls them Tilts and have other goals for the Conditions system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}